1
00:00:04,570 --> 00:00:06,940
We at least survived one day.
We're not going home today.

2
00:00:06,940 --> 00:00:08,040
Let's survive tomorrow as well.

3
00:00:08,040 --> 00:00:09,310
- Let's survive tomorrow as well.
- Right.

4
00:00:09,480 --> 00:00:11,310
- It's so...
- Let's do our best tomorrow...

5
00:00:11,850 --> 00:00:13,450
- and survive the next day as well.
- Okay.

6
00:00:13,450 --> 00:00:15,120
Even if we're just living day to day,

7
00:00:15,120 --> 00:00:16,920
- staying alive is what matters.
- That's right.

8
00:00:17,890 --> 00:00:19,220
Did the other teams
come to submit their lives?

9
00:00:20,460 --> 00:00:22,160
Is Team Red submitting first?

10
00:00:22,860 --> 00:00:24,030
- Oh, okay.
- So it shows like that...

11
00:00:24,030 --> 00:00:25,130
when it's being used.

12
00:00:25,130 --> 00:00:26,530
- They were quick.
- Right.

13
00:00:27,430 --> 00:00:29,630
Please check the contents
of the central box...

14
00:00:30,230 --> 00:00:34,040
and assign lives
to the residents of your choice.

15
00:00:37,240 --> 00:00:39,970
(Life Submission for Day 1)

16
00:00:44,080 --> 00:00:46,850
(Maillard)

17
00:00:48,920 --> 00:00:49,980
(Life Submission for Day 1)

18
00:00:51,720 --> 00:00:54,190
(All members of Team Red survived.)

19
00:00:54,790 --> 00:00:57,030
Your life submission is complete.

20
00:00:57,290 --> 00:00:59,290
You may now leave.

21
00:01:00,160 --> 00:01:01,900
I was actually considering it earlier.

22
00:01:01,900 --> 00:01:04,270
(Maillard, cooking YouTuber)

23
00:01:04,270 --> 00:01:07,000
I could kill the other members
if I wanted to.

24
00:01:07,640 --> 00:01:10,440
Under the current rules,
if only one member is left on a team,

25
00:01:10,570 --> 00:01:12,340
they no longer need any life.

26
00:01:12,570 --> 00:01:14,910
The leader can always end up on their own.

27
00:01:15,410 --> 00:01:18,350
But I don't think
there are only advantages to that.

28
00:01:18,680 --> 00:01:19,910
It's still the first day,

29
00:01:20,050 --> 00:01:22,320
and I don't know what more is out there.

30
00:01:22,980 --> 00:01:26,390
And making that decision
could really isolate me,

31
00:01:26,390 --> 00:01:28,790
so I didn't sabotage it.

32
00:01:29,120 --> 00:01:30,730
I considered it a little.

33
00:01:32,730 --> 00:01:35,060
- How many bathrooms are there?
- Two.

34
00:01:35,430 --> 00:01:36,530
- That wouldn't take long then.
- How nice.

35
00:01:36,530 --> 00:01:37,570
How many do you have?

36
00:01:37,570 --> 00:01:38,800
- Three?
- We have three.

37
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:42,200
Well done.

38
00:01:42,340 --> 00:01:44,310
Congratulations on surviving today.

39
00:01:44,310 --> 00:01:45,310
Let's see each other for a long time.

40
00:01:45,310 --> 00:01:46,810
The leader might not submit all the lives.

41
00:01:47,340 --> 00:01:49,710
- You'd be dead then.
- That's so mean.

42
00:01:49,710 --> 00:01:52,050
The leader could really choose
not to submit all of them.

43
00:01:52,380 --> 00:01:55,180
I'll be the one killing everyone?
Goodness.

44
00:01:55,180 --> 00:01:57,790
But to be able to come up
with that idea...

45
00:01:58,150 --> 00:02:00,050
makes them different from me.

46
00:02:00,050 --> 00:02:02,590
- Of course. You're a White.
- It didn't even cross my mind.

47
00:02:04,290 --> 00:02:06,230
They're good at coming up
with cruel ideas.

48
00:02:06,230 --> 00:02:09,800
Right. I guess you can see it
when you go in. The names and all.

49
00:02:09,930 --> 00:02:10,930
I guess so.

50
00:02:11,230 --> 00:02:13,370
Please check the contents
of the central box...

51
00:02:13,840 --> 00:02:17,640
and assign lives
to the residents of your choice.

52
00:02:19,010 --> 00:02:22,240
This really holds our lives.

53
00:02:24,180 --> 00:02:26,080
(Life Submission for Day 1: Genie)

54
00:02:27,050 --> 00:02:28,080
There.

55
00:02:28,520 --> 00:02:29,620
A fake.

56
00:02:32,190 --> 00:02:34,920
Let's ace the games tomorrow.

57
00:02:35,120 --> 00:02:36,160
Go!

58
00:02:37,990 --> 00:02:40,160
Your life submission is complete.

59
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:41,460
(All members of Team Blue survived.)

60
00:02:41,800 --> 00:02:43,500
I didn't think much about it today.

61
00:02:43,560 --> 00:02:45,130
Honestly, there's no merit.

62
00:02:45,130 --> 00:02:47,440
If I get rid of the members today,

63
00:02:47,440 --> 00:02:48,800
our team would lack in numbers.

64
00:02:49,640 --> 00:02:53,910
But really, at that moment...

65
00:02:53,910 --> 00:02:57,040
I thought, "I should really
keep my position as the leader."

66
00:02:57,550 --> 00:02:59,850
It'll be over if the leader
doesn't place the life in my slot.

67
00:02:59,910 --> 00:03:02,080
That's somehow more powerful...

68
00:03:02,080 --> 00:03:04,450
than having an exemption card.

69
00:03:04,550 --> 00:03:06,290
The leader can decide...

70
00:03:06,290 --> 00:03:08,920
whether or not to keep someone alive...

71
00:03:08,990 --> 00:03:11,190
during the submission.

72
00:03:11,190 --> 00:03:13,560
So I thought being a leader...

73
00:03:13,560 --> 00:03:16,260
was quite important.

74
00:03:18,900 --> 00:03:23,240
More than the perks of being a leader,

75
00:03:23,440 --> 00:03:27,310
I felt a responsibility
to take care of my team.

76
00:03:27,610 --> 00:03:30,410
I didn't think that was a privilege.

77
00:03:30,680 --> 00:03:31,780
Leia,

78
00:03:32,310 --> 00:03:33,310
Luna,

79
00:03:33,750 --> 00:03:35,720
Paul, Boss,

80
00:03:36,220 --> 00:03:37,920
Siseon, and Hamlet.

81
00:03:38,550 --> 00:03:39,720
Let's survive.

82
00:03:42,660 --> 00:03:44,960
Your life submission is complete.

83
00:03:45,960 --> 00:03:48,060
We all survived!

84
00:03:48,060 --> 00:03:50,260
- Well done.
- This is fun.

85
00:03:50,400 --> 00:03:52,470
I think becoming a leader
on the first day was a good decision...

86
00:03:52,470 --> 00:03:54,000
because I got to experience such things.

87
00:03:54,700 --> 00:03:57,210
It's quite fun to submit the resources.

88
00:03:57,210 --> 00:03:58,940
- Really?
- Submitting the diamonds and all.

89
00:04:02,840 --> 00:04:06,580
(Morning of Day 2)

90
00:04:06,850 --> 00:04:08,050
Would you like a cup of coffee?

91
00:04:08,050 --> 00:04:09,080
(Dormitory for White)

92
00:04:09,080 --> 00:04:10,950
- You said you needed a caffeine fix.
- Right.

93
00:04:10,950 --> 00:04:12,590
- Okay.
- I should, right?

94
00:04:13,250 --> 00:04:14,460
It smells so nice.

95
00:04:17,120 --> 00:04:19,090
The coffee smells nice.

96
00:04:19,560 --> 00:04:21,500
- Have some of this.
- Okay.

97
00:04:21,500 --> 00:04:22,860
- We have to work.
- Right.

98
00:04:23,030 --> 00:04:25,670
We can't be sure if we'll be able
to buy lunch this afternoon.

99
00:04:25,670 --> 00:04:27,540
Right. This could be our last meal.

100
00:04:28,570 --> 00:04:30,540
They'll give us food, at least.

101
00:04:31,270 --> 00:04:32,840
- Thank you for the coffee.
- Thank you.

102
00:04:32,840 --> 00:04:34,080
You can have that.

103
00:04:34,310 --> 00:04:35,780
I didn't have breakfast.

104
00:04:36,140 --> 00:04:38,780
Inflation doesn't just affect the economy.

105
00:04:38,780 --> 00:04:41,180
It affects our dopamine levels
and appetite too.

106
00:04:41,620 --> 00:04:43,680
If we get into the habit
of eating like this,

107
00:04:43,920 --> 00:04:46,650
we're going to lose it later on...

108
00:04:46,650 --> 00:04:47,990
when the snack bar closes
or we run out of money.

109
00:04:48,320 --> 00:04:50,790
So I wanted to get used to it.

110
00:04:50,990 --> 00:04:52,290
(Dormitory for Red)

111
00:04:52,290 --> 00:04:53,960
I wonder what we'll be producing.

112
00:04:54,700 --> 00:04:58,400
Since there are many days to get through,
there'll obviously be things like quizzes.

113
00:05:04,540 --> 00:05:06,240
I hope we're not going to that greenhouse.

114
00:05:07,240 --> 00:05:08,280
Right.

115
00:05:08,280 --> 00:05:10,540
- Start producing.
- In the real way.

116
00:05:10,650 --> 00:05:12,850
Credits will be awarded
based on the weight...

117
00:05:12,850 --> 00:05:14,250
of what you produce.

118
00:05:15,220 --> 00:05:18,350
Just off the top of your head,

119
00:05:18,920 --> 00:05:21,890
do you think Team Blue will give out
more than ten lives?

120
00:05:21,920 --> 00:05:23,790
They should. We're 13 people.

121
00:05:23,790 --> 00:05:25,490
They should distribute at least ten...

122
00:05:25,760 --> 00:05:28,160
for us to survive the remaining days.

123
00:05:28,700 --> 00:05:30,800
- Right?
- Yes.

124
00:05:31,330 --> 00:05:34,000
In the worst case, we might all be
heading home the day after tomorrow.

125
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:35,170
That's the worst scenario.

126
00:05:35,270 --> 00:05:37,170
Right. If they keep the lives.

127
00:05:37,170 --> 00:05:40,880
Then, should we collect lives on our own?

128
00:05:41,480 --> 00:05:43,340
Yes. We'll check out their stance today,

129
00:05:43,340 --> 00:05:45,750
and if they're not willing to budge,

130
00:05:45,750 --> 00:05:47,980
we'll just have to work hard tomorrow...

131
00:05:47,980 --> 00:05:49,450
and find a way to get some lives.

132
00:05:49,920 --> 00:05:50,920
(Dormitory for Blue)

133
00:05:50,920 --> 00:05:52,720
I think giving out the lives...

134
00:05:53,120 --> 00:05:56,290
one-for-one yesterday didn't make sense.

135
00:05:56,290 --> 00:05:59,430
There wouldn't be so many lives.

136
00:05:59,890 --> 00:06:03,100
It couldn't be helped since
we were feeling things out yesterday.

137
00:06:04,200 --> 00:06:09,170
Team Red can still take it easy
at least for today.

138
00:06:09,840 --> 00:06:12,010
Team White is the one without lives.

139
00:06:12,010 --> 00:06:14,040
Team White will just live for today.

140
00:06:14,040 --> 00:06:15,780
They're barely getting by.

141
00:06:16,010 --> 00:06:19,550
Either way, at least through today,

142
00:06:19,550 --> 00:06:21,220
they pretty much have to trade with us.

143
00:06:21,850 --> 00:06:24,090
We went for it yesterday, so today...

144
00:06:24,090 --> 00:06:26,650
- We have to play it safe today.
- At least...

145
00:06:26,650 --> 00:06:28,990
We should secure the three lives
we're going to take first...

146
00:06:28,990 --> 00:06:31,130
We might earn more. If we earn more...

147
00:06:31,130 --> 00:06:32,560
For example, if we end up
with more than three,

148
00:06:32,560 --> 00:06:35,430
we could sell those.

149
00:06:35,430 --> 00:06:36,530
Right.

150
00:06:36,830 --> 00:06:39,130
Also, I think...

151
00:06:39,730 --> 00:06:42,370
we should pretend we're not making much.

152
00:06:43,070 --> 00:06:44,410
Act like we don't have so many lives.

153
00:06:44,410 --> 00:06:45,970
- Right.
- That way...

154
00:06:46,070 --> 00:06:48,280
- That way, Team White...
- We can negotiate a higher price.

155
00:06:48,280 --> 00:06:50,610
There's definitely going to come
a day when the lives become worthless.

156
00:06:50,610 --> 00:06:51,780
Right.

157
00:06:52,150 --> 00:06:53,610
Before they become worthless,

158
00:06:53,610 --> 00:06:55,450
- we need to sell them for a high price...
- Right.

159
00:06:55,650 --> 00:06:58,320
around the middle of the game.

160
00:06:58,450 --> 00:07:01,560
But we really don't know what to expect
from Team White's money issuance.

161
00:07:01,560 --> 00:07:03,060
It's a big unknown.

162
00:07:03,220 --> 00:07:04,560
- Because...
- It's not fair.

163
00:07:04,560 --> 00:07:08,900
They can't issue them
right after we've made our deal.

164
00:07:08,900 --> 00:07:10,330
- That shouldn't happen.
- Right.

165
00:07:10,970 --> 00:07:13,470
Our team's survival
is pretty much secured,

166
00:07:13,630 --> 00:07:16,140
so I should start going
after some prize money.

167
00:07:16,370 --> 00:07:20,670
But since Team White has complete control
over the diamonds,

168
00:07:20,670 --> 00:07:23,840
I was really wondering
how they're going to issue them...

169
00:07:23,840 --> 00:07:25,180
and how the whole system is going to work.

170
00:07:25,810 --> 00:07:27,680
You have to keep...

171
00:07:27,680 --> 00:07:30,120
whoever has a monopoly in check.

172
00:07:30,790 --> 00:07:33,390
We should talk about that well...

173
00:07:33,390 --> 00:07:34,720
- in advance, right?
- Right.

174
00:07:35,020 --> 00:07:39,190
I was thinking maybe we should try
working with the other teams.

175
00:07:39,190 --> 00:07:40,630
It's true that we need
to issue currency now...

176
00:07:40,630 --> 00:07:43,200
to keep things flowing smoothly.

177
00:07:43,300 --> 00:07:46,730
Right now, each diamond
is worth 1,000 dollars, and that's huge.

178
00:07:46,800 --> 00:07:48,170
So we need to issue currency.

179
00:07:48,170 --> 00:07:49,700
But if we start
issuing currency recklessly,

180
00:07:49,700 --> 00:07:51,210
the other teams could get suspicious...

181
00:07:51,210 --> 00:07:53,340
and we could also start
mistrusting each other.

182
00:07:53,340 --> 00:07:54,810
We can tell them that and say,

183
00:07:54,810 --> 00:07:57,210
"We'll make an announcement
like the Bank of Korea."

184
00:07:57,550 --> 00:08:00,080
In return, we'll ask them to guarantee
our survival...

185
00:08:00,080 --> 00:08:01,950
and our credits,
which give us the right to work.

186
00:08:02,080 --> 00:08:05,820
I think we should make our deal
based on the fact...

187
00:08:06,190 --> 00:08:08,920
that we work most efficiently
when all six of us are working together.

188
00:08:09,190 --> 00:08:11,260
I think issuing too many diamonds...

189
00:08:11,260 --> 00:08:14,430
could cause some confusion.

190
00:08:14,700 --> 00:08:17,130
So we're trying to make sure
we communicate that well...

191
00:08:17,130 --> 00:08:19,570
to the other teams in advance,

192
00:08:19,570 --> 00:08:20,940
so we can rebuild trust...

193
00:08:20,940 --> 00:08:23,440
without causing too much disruption
to prices.

194
00:08:23,940 --> 00:08:25,710
That's what we're aiming for.

195
00:08:26,040 --> 00:08:28,610
If we issued too much,

196
00:08:28,610 --> 00:08:31,410
it could break the trust
between the teams.

197
00:08:31,910 --> 00:08:34,580
Since we needed to secure enough lives,

198
00:08:34,580 --> 00:08:35,980
it was more important to show
that we can be trusted.

199
00:08:36,680 --> 00:08:38,750
If they don't agree with this,

200
00:08:38,920 --> 00:08:40,390
we could say, "We'll increase
the amount of currency in circulation..."

201
00:08:40,390 --> 00:08:43,360
"beyond a certain limit
and not say anything."

202
00:08:43,520 --> 00:08:45,630
I think that could be our greatest weapon.

203
00:08:46,430 --> 00:08:48,160
That's our greatest and only weapon.

204
00:08:48,160 --> 00:08:49,230
It's our only weapon.

205
00:08:49,230 --> 00:08:51,200
How transparent...

206
00:08:51,200 --> 00:08:52,500
are we talking about?

207
00:08:52,500 --> 00:08:53,900
We'll keep the amount
of currency we issue...

208
00:08:53,900 --> 00:08:56,240
- within a certain limit.
- For example, we'll increase...

209
00:08:56,240 --> 00:08:58,340
- the money supply by 10 percent a day.
- We'll increase it by 10 percent.

210
00:08:58,340 --> 00:08:59,340
- We'll do that.
- That much.

211
00:08:59,340 --> 00:09:00,370
Do you want us to set a rule like that?

212
00:09:00,640 --> 00:09:02,480
- And announce it to them?
- We'll announce it to them.

213
00:09:02,580 --> 00:09:04,810
But one thing we absolutely
shouldn't tell them...

214
00:09:04,810 --> 00:09:06,250
- is that there's a limit.
- Right.

215
00:09:06,810 --> 00:09:07,850
(Last night)

216
00:09:07,850 --> 00:09:08,980
Everyone.

217
00:09:09,450 --> 00:09:11,690
It's written here that we can issue...

218
00:09:11,690 --> 00:09:13,490
up to 200 additional diamonds once a day.

219
00:09:13,490 --> 00:09:15,090
- Once per person.
- Once per person.

220
00:09:15,090 --> 00:09:16,720
- Once a day?
- Once a day.

221
00:09:16,990 --> 00:09:19,560
Starting on Day Two,
Team White can submit...

222
00:09:19,560 --> 00:09:21,030
the provided diamond issuance voucher...

223
00:09:21,030 --> 00:09:23,860
during Community Center hours...

224
00:09:24,130 --> 00:09:27,100
and issue up to 200 additional diamonds...

225
00:09:27,100 --> 00:09:29,470
once per day.

226
00:09:29,800 --> 00:09:33,040
No credits are required
to issue additional diamonds.

227
00:09:33,470 --> 00:09:35,040
That means we can't make
the value of the currency drop so much...

228
00:09:35,040 --> 00:09:36,980
- The voucher...
- as we get further into the game.

229
00:09:37,040 --> 00:09:38,180
- Because we can issue...
- That's right.

230
00:09:38,180 --> 00:09:39,410
- only up to 200 diamonds per day.
- That's right.

231
00:09:39,750 --> 00:09:41,480
- Right.
- We can only make it drop at first.

232
00:09:41,480 --> 00:09:43,780
It won't fall so much from the next day.

233
00:09:44,320 --> 00:09:45,590
We also don't need to put...

234
00:09:45,590 --> 00:09:46,850
- a lot into circulation early on.
- That's right.

235
00:09:46,850 --> 00:09:48,190
If we keep the money supply low
at the beginning...

236
00:09:48,190 --> 00:09:50,190
and increase it little by little,

237
00:09:50,190 --> 00:09:52,960
then if we suddenly issue
200 a day right at the end,

238
00:09:52,960 --> 00:09:55,000
the value is going to drop by almost half.

239
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:56,230
We should make use of that.

240
00:09:56,230 --> 00:09:57,300
- That's right.
- Yes.

241
00:09:57,630 --> 00:10:00,870
What percentage should we promise
to increase it by in the beginning?

242
00:10:00,870 --> 00:10:02,570
So I think...

243
00:10:02,570 --> 00:10:05,340
- By ten percent?
- we should check the prices first.

244
00:10:05,340 --> 00:10:07,010
- The prices.
- We should check...

245
00:10:07,010 --> 00:10:08,380
the current market prices.

246
00:10:08,380 --> 00:10:10,280
- Right. The prices...
- How much Black is selling them for.

247
00:10:10,480 --> 00:10:12,650
We also need to check
how many lives and credits...

248
00:10:12,650 --> 00:10:15,680
- we can actually produce.
- That's right.

249
00:10:15,780 --> 00:10:16,920
That's right.

250
00:10:17,590 --> 00:10:20,820
We're going to have lunch
after the game, right?

251
00:10:20,820 --> 00:10:25,130
Yes. It will be lunchtime.
We should buy it from Vector.

252
00:10:25,630 --> 00:10:28,630
I think if we stay...

253
00:10:28,630 --> 00:10:30,530
on good terms with Vector,

254
00:10:30,730 --> 00:10:34,070
we could get a lot of information
for free.

255
00:10:34,070 --> 00:10:37,270
But Vector's friendliness
could also be calculated.

256
00:10:37,940 --> 00:10:40,110
- I think he's that kind of character.
- That's possible.

257
00:10:40,340 --> 00:10:43,110
Just accumulating a lot of diamonds
is a little too one-dimensional.

258
00:10:43,110 --> 00:10:45,280
I feel like there's something more to it.

259
00:10:45,280 --> 00:10:46,350
Right.

260
00:10:47,350 --> 00:10:48,520
What could that be?

261
00:10:48,950 --> 00:10:50,720
It's not about collecting many diamonds.

262
00:10:52,850 --> 00:10:55,420
Maillard is certain
that it's not about collecting diamonds.

263
00:10:56,520 --> 00:10:59,460
No one did a better job of winning
people over yesterday than Vector.

264
00:10:59,630 --> 00:11:01,560
He really won everyone over yesterday.

265
00:11:01,660 --> 00:11:04,060
He's the only person
who went around to every team...

266
00:11:04,260 --> 00:11:07,430
and won people over.

267
00:11:07,740 --> 00:11:09,800
Honestly, I think whoever gets Vector
on their side...

268
00:11:09,800 --> 00:11:12,640
has the biggest advantage.

269
00:11:12,640 --> 00:11:14,440
There are six members here,

270
00:11:14,440 --> 00:11:15,580
- Right.
- and it doesn't feel like...

271
00:11:15,580 --> 00:11:16,710
we've completely...

272
00:11:16,710 --> 00:11:19,050
- clicked with the three Team Red members.
- Exactly.

273
00:11:19,250 --> 00:11:22,120
To succeed in winning over Team Red,

274
00:11:22,120 --> 00:11:23,250
we must use this very person.

275
00:11:23,350 --> 00:11:24,450
- True.
- Right?

276
00:11:24,620 --> 00:11:25,650
- He's sly.
- Yes.

277
00:11:25,650 --> 00:11:27,690
- Very.
- He is.

278
00:11:27,690 --> 00:11:28,760
- He's sly.
- Right?

279
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:41,570
(The Community 2: Invisible Hand)

280
00:11:42,440 --> 00:11:45,740
(2: When We Want the Same Thing)

281
00:11:46,040 --> 00:11:48,310
Day Two has begun.

282
00:11:48,910 --> 00:11:51,110
Team leaders can now be changed...

283
00:11:51,310 --> 00:11:53,680
at the Community Center.

284
00:11:54,110 --> 00:11:57,950
Discuss whether to reappoint
the current leader.

285
00:11:58,190 --> 00:11:59,990
What matters is whether anyone wants...

286
00:11:59,990 --> 00:12:01,120
- to become the leader.
- True.

287
00:12:01,620 --> 00:12:04,730
If anyone wants to become the leader,
please speak up.

288
00:12:04,730 --> 00:12:06,960
Was there any benefit to being the leader?

289
00:12:07,930 --> 00:12:09,460
- Being one feels good?
- No.

290
00:12:10,300 --> 00:12:11,430
- No.
- Maybe this much?

291
00:12:11,430 --> 00:12:13,730
- This badge.
- I see, so it's the badge.

292
00:12:15,470 --> 00:12:16,570
Do you want to be one?

293
00:12:16,600 --> 00:12:17,710
No, I'm fine.

294
00:12:17,810 --> 00:12:19,510
How about we have her serve again?

295
00:12:19,640 --> 00:12:22,310
I prefer chirping away as just a member.

296
00:12:22,310 --> 00:12:23,440
It seems like it.

297
00:12:24,650 --> 00:12:27,010
I support Luna.

298
00:12:27,010 --> 00:12:28,980
- Same here.
- I support her.

299
00:12:29,720 --> 00:12:31,890
- Shall we show off our unity?
- Okay.

300
00:12:31,890 --> 00:12:32,920
(Team White's leader
has been reappointed.)

301
00:12:32,920 --> 00:12:34,220
- Great.
- Good.

302
00:12:35,320 --> 00:12:37,020
How about reappointing him?

303
00:12:37,360 --> 00:12:40,190
I totally agree with that.

304
00:12:40,590 --> 00:12:43,200
Changing our leader
didn't even cross my mind...

305
00:12:43,200 --> 00:12:49,070
because Maillard made trades yesterday
very adamantly.

306
00:12:49,070 --> 00:12:51,510
So, I thought he should continue
being the leader...

307
00:12:51,510 --> 00:12:52,940
and didn't have a second thought about it.

308
00:12:53,370 --> 00:12:54,880
- Maillard.
- Yes?

309
00:12:54,880 --> 00:12:56,740
- I love you being the leader.
- Totally.

310
00:12:57,280 --> 00:12:58,880
I know, right? It's reassuring.

311
00:12:59,580 --> 00:13:00,580
However,

312
00:13:01,180 --> 00:13:03,920
neither the power...

313
00:13:04,120 --> 00:13:07,190
nor the role of the leader
has been revealed completely.

314
00:13:07,350 --> 00:13:10,620
That feeling of holding
the power of life and death...

315
00:13:10,620 --> 00:13:12,260
when submitting the life at night is...

316
00:13:12,560 --> 00:13:16,500
Should I suggest taking turns
as the leader?

317
00:13:16,660 --> 00:13:20,630
But bringing it up right now
in this situation...

318
00:13:20,930 --> 00:13:22,970
might arouse unnecessary suspicions.

319
00:13:23,270 --> 00:13:24,970
I didn't have any reason.

320
00:13:25,410 --> 00:13:26,840
Who wants to be the leader today?

321
00:13:27,470 --> 00:13:28,780
- Salt.
- Me today?

322
00:13:28,780 --> 00:13:30,080
- Go ahead.
- Yes.

323
00:13:30,080 --> 00:13:31,680
All right, I'll be the leader today.

324
00:13:31,950 --> 00:13:33,210
- Decided.
- Decided.

325
00:13:33,210 --> 00:13:34,680
(Team Blue's leader: Salt)

326
00:13:34,850 --> 00:13:37,550
Our team decided to take turns,

327
00:13:37,820 --> 00:13:40,650
so it wasn't a matter of satisfaction
and whatnot.

328
00:13:41,590 --> 00:13:43,560
I like this system.

329
00:13:43,990 --> 00:13:47,030
At this rate,
we'll just keep taking turns.

330
00:13:47,290 --> 00:13:51,500
I wasn't sure if it was efficient.

331
00:13:51,700 --> 00:13:55,440
I'm thinking of taking the role.

332
00:13:56,170 --> 00:13:57,670
We need to head to the Community Center.

333
00:13:57,670 --> 00:13:59,570
- Is that where we announce the leader?
- Yes.

334
00:14:00,210 --> 00:14:02,580
- I'm off.
- Bye.

335
00:14:02,840 --> 00:14:05,650
(Team Red's Day 2 leader: Maillard)

336
00:14:05,750 --> 00:14:08,120
(Team White's Day 2 leader: Luna)

337
00:14:08,120 --> 00:14:10,250
(Team Black's Day 2 leader: Vector)

338
00:14:10,450 --> 00:14:11,950
Collect the Day Two schedule...

339
00:14:12,220 --> 00:14:14,960
from the central box.

340
00:14:17,190 --> 00:14:19,360
(Community Center)

341
00:14:20,330 --> 00:14:21,430
Hi.

342
00:14:21,760 --> 00:14:24,130
- Hi.
- Hi.

343
00:14:24,130 --> 00:14:25,700
Are you reappointing the leader?

344
00:14:25,700 --> 00:14:27,700
- No, we're changing.
- No, ours change every day.

345
00:14:27,700 --> 00:14:29,440
- Turns.
- Our plan is to take turns.

346
00:14:29,440 --> 00:14:31,000
- We're taking turns.
- Could we...

347
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:33,610
- talk outside for a minute?
- Sure. Got it.

348
00:14:34,170 --> 00:14:36,080
If you wish to change your leader,

349
00:14:36,510 --> 00:14:39,110
please state the name of the new leader.

350
00:14:39,910 --> 00:14:42,350
We'd like to change the leader to Salt.

351
00:14:43,320 --> 00:14:47,220
The new leader is to collect
the instructions from the central box.

352
00:14:48,490 --> 00:14:49,860
Here are some instructions.

353
00:14:50,820 --> 00:14:52,530
- Production rules.
- Production rules.

354
00:14:52,730 --> 00:14:55,560
Starting Day Two, every team can earn...

355
00:14:55,560 --> 00:14:58,000
lives or credits
through productive activities.

356
00:14:58,200 --> 00:15:00,970
Submit one credit at the production site,

357
00:15:01,870 --> 00:15:05,610
and you will receive
ten production questions per day.

358
00:15:06,570 --> 00:15:08,040
If you want a hint,

359
00:15:08,040 --> 00:15:09,940
A hint, please.

360
00:15:09,940 --> 00:15:12,210
an additional credit is required.

361
00:15:13,180 --> 00:15:16,180
If you wish to retry
after an incorrect answer,

362
00:15:16,180 --> 00:15:17,520
We'd like to retry.

363
00:15:17,580 --> 00:15:19,820
you must also pay an additional credit.

364
00:15:20,920 --> 00:15:24,020
During production activities,
the amount of resources...

365
00:15:24,020 --> 00:15:26,260
each team can receive varies.

366
00:15:27,930 --> 00:15:31,830
"If Team White chooses to produce
lives or credits,"

367
00:15:32,430 --> 00:15:35,270
"one life or credit is produced
for every three correct answers."

368
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:38,510
"If the team answers
all ten questions correctly,"

369
00:15:38,510 --> 00:15:41,010
"they will produce
a total of five lives or credits."

370
00:15:44,480 --> 00:15:46,310
- Three questions.
- One per three questions.

371
00:15:46,950 --> 00:15:48,850
The return is terrible.

372
00:15:49,580 --> 00:15:50,980
It's really terrible.

373
00:15:52,020 --> 00:15:55,560
This is bad.
Looking at the ratio, it's 3-to-1.

374
00:15:55,560 --> 00:15:57,120
We have to solve 3 just to get 1,

375
00:15:57,120 --> 00:15:58,890
and the questions
definitely won't be easy.

376
00:15:59,430 --> 00:16:01,360
If we...

377
00:16:01,360 --> 00:16:03,430
do really well, maybe we can get three?

378
00:16:03,700 --> 00:16:05,830
Wouldn't getting two be enough
to break even?

379
00:16:05,830 --> 00:16:07,900
It's very upsetting and unreasonable.

380
00:16:08,440 --> 00:16:10,070
The production efficiency is way too low.

381
00:16:10,070 --> 00:16:13,110
Is such a low production efficiency
even right with this many people?

382
00:16:13,970 --> 00:16:17,540
If only we could receive
a bit more generosity, you know?

383
00:16:18,150 --> 00:16:19,610
Do you think it's the same
for the other teams?

384
00:16:20,180 --> 00:16:22,180
The amount must be different
for each team.

385
00:16:22,320 --> 00:16:23,880
- Credits? Right.
- For example,

386
00:16:23,880 --> 00:16:26,190
get 1 question right,
and that team gets 1 resource right away.

387
00:16:26,790 --> 00:16:29,620
Could the ratio be 3-to-1 for us
and 1-to-1 for them?

388
00:16:29,620 --> 00:16:30,860
Maybe.

389
00:16:31,690 --> 00:16:34,090
"If Team Blue chooses to produce lives,"

390
00:16:34,090 --> 00:16:35,630
- "one life is produced..."
- We've got...

391
00:16:35,630 --> 00:16:37,200
- "for every correct answer."
- a great deal.

392
00:16:37,460 --> 00:16:38,930
"If the team chooses to produce credits,"

393
00:16:38,930 --> 00:16:41,840
"one credit is produced
for every three correct answers."

394
00:16:42,400 --> 00:16:44,400
The 3-to-1 ratio was correct.

395
00:16:44,710 --> 00:16:47,810
It's only reasonable for us
to produce lives.

396
00:16:47,910 --> 00:16:49,480
- Exactly.
- I told you.

397
00:16:49,480 --> 00:16:51,810
- The ratio of lives can't be 1-to-1.
- But...

398
00:16:51,810 --> 00:16:54,580
Since yesterday, I kept saying...

399
00:16:54,680 --> 00:16:57,120
how one credit could not be
the same as one life.

400
00:16:57,380 --> 00:17:01,020
Even at the lowest,
it's one credit per team,

401
00:17:01,020 --> 00:17:03,790
which gets you a minimum ratio of 3-to-1.

402
00:17:04,020 --> 00:17:06,560
Credits were mentioned as opportunities.

403
00:17:06,790 --> 00:17:10,560
The opportunity must be to earn lives.

404
00:17:10,960 --> 00:17:12,970
If you think about it logically,

405
00:17:12,970 --> 00:17:15,570
such a ratio is impossible.

406
00:17:15,570 --> 00:17:18,770
Either way, we traded five lives.

407
00:17:19,470 --> 00:17:21,580
One credit is worth...

408
00:17:21,580 --> 00:17:24,110
a huge number of lives.

409
00:17:25,050 --> 00:17:27,910
We really got the short end of the stick.

410
00:17:29,520 --> 00:17:33,890
There is a limited total supply of lives
that can be produced.

411
00:17:34,520 --> 00:17:38,530
This supply is shared across
the entire Community Town,

412
00:17:39,160 --> 00:17:43,330
so even if multiple teams
produce lives independently,

413
00:17:43,830 --> 00:17:46,100
they are all deducted
from the same shared pool.

414
00:17:46,100 --> 00:17:48,070
(Total life supply)

415
00:17:48,340 --> 00:17:49,440
Goodness.

416
00:17:49,440 --> 00:17:52,110
If the life supply holds a total of 10,
the other team produces 5,

417
00:17:52,240 --> 00:17:54,510
and we produce 3, only 2 are left.

418
00:17:55,780 --> 00:17:56,910
That's tough.

419
00:17:57,440 --> 00:17:59,080
- The production rules are absurd.
- I see.

420
00:18:00,250 --> 00:18:02,420
The ratio is hard to believe.

421
00:18:03,080 --> 00:18:05,120
Get 1 question right,
and we get 3 credits.

422
00:18:06,350 --> 00:18:08,290
Get 3 questions right, and we get 1 life.

423
00:18:08,920 --> 00:18:10,320
One per three answers?

424
00:18:10,320 --> 00:18:12,530
Get 6 right, and we'd get 2 lives.

425
00:18:12,530 --> 00:18:13,690
Right now...

426
00:18:14,060 --> 00:18:15,460
Now that I'm looking at it,

427
00:18:15,460 --> 00:18:16,830
- the ratio is 9-to-1.
- You're right.

428
00:18:16,830 --> 00:18:18,230
Right? It's 9-to-1.

429
00:18:18,230 --> 00:18:19,800
This ratio is crazy.

430
00:18:20,400 --> 00:18:23,070
It's close to the 10-to-1 ratio
we had guessed.

431
00:18:23,070 --> 00:18:24,540
- Is that so?
- Yes, it's 9-to-1.

432
00:18:25,070 --> 00:18:26,070
- Oh, my.
- Exactly.

433
00:18:26,070 --> 00:18:28,510
- In short, we use...
- Yes?

434
00:18:29,540 --> 00:18:31,780
one credit to get ten questions...

435
00:18:31,780 --> 00:18:34,210
- and use about 5 to 6 credits...
- Yes?

436
00:18:34,780 --> 00:18:36,450
- for the hint or to retry.
- Right.

437
00:18:36,720 --> 00:18:40,390
We could earn about 7 credits and 2 lives.

438
00:18:40,420 --> 00:18:43,390
Gosh, the ratio is out of this world.

439
00:18:43,560 --> 00:18:47,190
Or we could use 7 credits
and earn 21 credits.

440
00:18:47,190 --> 00:18:48,630
That feels right.

441
00:18:50,700 --> 00:18:53,030
- All done?
- Hi.

442
00:18:53,030 --> 00:18:54,370
Why do you look shocked?

443
00:18:54,530 --> 00:18:56,570
- It's nothing.
- There's so much information,

444
00:18:56,570 --> 00:18:58,140
- so my brain isn't working.
- Is that so?

445
00:19:00,710 --> 00:19:01,980
Well...

446
00:19:02,510 --> 00:19:04,010
- If I'm being completely honest...
- Yes?

447
00:19:04,380 --> 00:19:06,410
- You don't have any lives, do you?
- I need lives.

448
00:19:06,410 --> 00:19:07,480
Right.

449
00:19:07,880 --> 00:19:11,650
(During last night's life submission)

450
00:19:12,590 --> 00:19:18,760
(1 life is needed to run the supermarket
for a day.)

451
00:19:19,490 --> 00:19:23,230
(Vector submits the 1 life he had.)

452
00:19:26,870 --> 00:19:28,500
To run it the next day...

453
00:19:30,500 --> 00:19:31,840
How do I get a life?

454
00:19:33,710 --> 00:19:35,040
But we can't trade.

455
00:19:35,510 --> 00:19:38,910
So I did a lot of thinking yesterday.

456
00:19:39,110 --> 00:19:42,220
I had zero lives today.

457
00:19:42,320 --> 00:19:45,420
I thought long and hard about
how to earn lives.

458
00:19:45,650 --> 00:19:47,420
No matter how much I read the rule book,

459
00:19:47,520 --> 00:19:50,020
I couldn't trade for lives or credits.

460
00:19:50,560 --> 00:19:52,560
I'd either have to be handed some over...

461
00:19:52,660 --> 00:19:55,700
or trade in a black market
outside the law.

462
00:19:56,300 --> 00:19:59,200
Since I can't trade for lives,
I have to earn them another way.

463
00:19:59,200 --> 00:20:02,570
So I'm going to create a black market.

464
00:20:03,140 --> 00:20:05,010
Is that possible?

465
00:20:05,010 --> 00:20:07,040
I don't know.
I'm just going to give it a shot.

466
00:20:07,510 --> 00:20:10,380
- What? A shot?
- Here's what I can offer.

467
00:20:10,380 --> 00:20:12,510
Give me a life, and in return,

468
00:20:12,510 --> 00:20:15,250
I will provide
whatever food you want for two days.

469
00:20:15,780 --> 00:20:18,020
If we agree to it...

470
00:20:18,450 --> 00:20:21,590
Under the assumption that
we have enough food,

471
00:20:21,660 --> 00:20:23,190
there's no benefit for us.

472
00:20:23,360 --> 00:20:26,390
Shouldn't we get a certain percentage
of the sales revenue?

473
00:20:26,560 --> 00:20:27,960
That way, we'd actually come out ahead.

474
00:20:28,230 --> 00:20:29,500
Do you not need food?

475
00:20:29,630 --> 00:20:32,300
It's not that necessary at the moment.

476
00:20:32,300 --> 00:20:34,300
- We can starve for hours.
- Exactly.

477
00:20:34,830 --> 00:20:36,940
- Starve for hours?
- I've been on a diet for a long time.

478
00:20:36,940 --> 00:20:39,210
- Coincidentally...
- I've been needing to go on a diet.

479
00:20:39,370 --> 00:20:40,910
I didn't see this coming.

480
00:20:41,170 --> 00:20:44,580
But even we don't know
how many lives we can produce.

481
00:20:44,580 --> 00:20:46,650
We'll find out only after
this production activity is over.

482
00:20:46,750 --> 00:20:49,680
We could talk about this again
after seeing how many we can produce...

483
00:20:49,680 --> 00:20:52,020
- and whether there's room to adjust...
- True.

484
00:20:52,020 --> 00:20:53,520
the percentage.

485
00:20:53,690 --> 00:20:55,690
- But...
- Frankly, food isn't important to us.

486
00:20:55,690 --> 00:20:58,460
- But we've talked about wanting...
- Yes?

487
00:20:58,460 --> 00:20:59,560
to get along with you.

488
00:20:59,560 --> 00:21:01,030
It really was a topic this morning.

489
00:21:01,630 --> 00:21:04,000
It wasn't something we really needed.

490
00:21:04,000 --> 00:21:06,830
But it was a step needed to form...

491
00:21:06,830 --> 00:21:08,300
a relationship with Black,

492
00:21:08,300 --> 00:21:11,170
so we were okay with it for that purpose.

493
00:21:11,270 --> 00:21:12,370
For now...

494
00:21:14,240 --> 00:21:16,480
I'll take it that
you're willing to make a deal.

495
00:21:16,480 --> 00:21:17,980
- Yes.
- That's for sure.

496
00:21:17,980 --> 00:21:19,850
Let's leave it at this.
We'll have the right to...

497
00:21:19,850 --> 00:21:21,010
- first distribution.
- Okay.

498
00:21:21,110 --> 00:21:22,420
Please save me.

499
00:21:23,120 --> 00:21:25,550
That depends on the deal we make.

500
00:21:25,550 --> 00:21:26,590
- For sure.
- What a power trip.

501
00:21:27,290 --> 00:21:29,660
- We'll think about it.
- Got it.

502
00:21:29,660 --> 00:21:31,660
- For now, take care.
- Take care.

503
00:21:34,160 --> 00:21:35,630
- That was cute, Pitou.
- Really.

504
00:21:35,930 --> 00:21:38,060
With a girly dress on, Pitou...

505
00:21:38,700 --> 00:21:41,740
- She's giving off cool gangster vibes.
- Right?

506
00:21:41,740 --> 00:21:43,800
- She's full of surprises.
- How much we can produce...

507
00:21:43,800 --> 00:21:45,370
- A woman full of surprises.
- is still a mystery.

508
00:21:45,370 --> 00:21:47,310
It's something to think about.

509
00:21:47,310 --> 00:21:50,810
We really need to think things through,
as some things are still unknown to us.

510
00:21:51,310 --> 00:21:53,310
- For now...
- For now, we'll see how things unfold.

511
