00:50:50,580 --> 00:50:52,650
- But...
- But it's too...

1277
00:50:52,850 --> 00:50:54,590
- That might be too easy.
- It's like SOS.

1278
00:50:54,590 --> 00:50:56,820
Right. The answer might be Morse code...

1279
00:50:57,020 --> 00:50:58,890
or a separate name for this.

1280
00:50:58,890 --> 00:51:00,490
- A separate name?
- Right.

1281
00:51:00,630 --> 00:51:03,060
We should clear things up
by checking the hint.

1282
00:51:03,060 --> 00:51:05,500
- Shall we check the hint?
- Since we have a lot?

1283
00:51:05,660 --> 00:51:08,930
Please insert one credit
into the credit box.

1284
00:51:09,730 --> 00:51:13,270
"It was used during the first experimental
long-distance telegraph line..."

1285
00:51:13,270 --> 00:51:14,870
"from Washington, D.C to Baltimore
in 1844."

1286
00:51:14,870 --> 00:51:16,670
Isn't it really Morse code?

1287
00:51:16,910 --> 00:51:19,880
I think I've read about this
from a biography.

1288
00:51:20,350 --> 00:51:22,010
Something Way? Faraway?

1289
00:51:22,110 --> 00:51:24,020
He dealt with electrochemistry.

1290
00:51:24,580 --> 00:51:27,620
Should we go with Morse code?
There's nothing else.

1291
00:51:27,750 --> 00:51:28,890
We don't have a different answer.

1292
00:51:29,490 --> 00:51:31,720
- Morse code...
- It does sound too obvious.

1293
00:51:31,720 --> 00:51:33,560
- sounds too obvious.
- Right.

1294
00:51:33,730 --> 00:51:35,030
Should we go with the Faraway signal?

1295
00:51:36,290 --> 00:51:38,930
The picture on top.

1296
00:51:38,930 --> 00:51:40,500
Isn't it really Morse code?

1297
00:51:40,530 --> 00:51:41,670
Let's go with Morse code.

1298
00:51:42,030 --> 00:51:43,030
Morse code.

1299
00:51:43,170 --> 00:51:45,500
I think it's simply just Morse code.

1300
00:51:46,240 --> 00:51:47,370
Morse code.

1301
00:51:47,870 --> 00:51:49,270
We will go with the Faraway signal.

1302
00:51:50,210 --> 00:51:51,240
That is incorrect.

1303
00:51:52,580 --> 00:51:53,910
What if it's Morse code?

1304
00:51:54,450 --> 00:51:56,050
- Shall we move on?
- Let's move on.

1305
00:51:56,050 --> 00:51:58,220
- Please don't be Morse code.
- Here's the answer.

1306
00:51:58,220 --> 00:51:59,250
Please!

1307
00:52:00,750 --> 00:52:02,420
- That is correct.
- That's right!

1308
00:52:03,050 --> 00:52:04,760
That's right!

1309
00:52:04,760 --> 00:52:06,620
- I said it from the start.
- Nice!

1310
00:52:11,460 --> 00:52:12,960
We thought too deeply.

1311
00:52:13,800 --> 00:52:16,630
- We shouldn't think too deeply.
- Right. We thought too deeply.

1312
00:52:16,630 --> 00:52:18,200
- This was a freebie.
- Right.

1313
00:52:18,200 --> 00:52:19,670
It was a freebie.

1314
00:52:20,370 --> 00:52:21,840
The questions earlier were hard.

1315
00:52:23,540 --> 00:52:24,680
"The leader is going to change tomorrow."

1316
00:52:26,310 --> 00:52:27,710
I think there will be a leader change.

1317
00:52:30,880 --> 00:52:33,180
There's nothing we can do.
Let's get the last question right.

1318
00:52:34,320 --> 00:52:35,720
Here's the last question.

1319
00:52:36,290 --> 00:52:38,620
"Official signatures
of country representatives?"

1320
00:52:39,290 --> 00:52:41,530
Isn't that "war with Japan?"

1321
00:52:41,690 --> 00:52:45,900
Supreme Commander for the Allied Powers.

1322
00:52:45,900 --> 00:52:47,800
That represents the allied countries.

1323
00:52:48,070 --> 00:52:50,540
Couldn't that be
the end of war declaration?

1324
00:52:50,770 --> 00:52:53,100
- "Geneva Conventions."
- Right.

1325
00:52:53,100 --> 00:52:55,810
- It's along those lines.
- It's along those lines.

1326
00:52:56,310 --> 00:52:57,510
What were the Geneva Conventions again?

1327
00:52:57,980 --> 00:52:59,710
So what is the name of that?

1328
00:52:59,880 --> 00:53:02,210
An end-of-war agreement?

1329
00:53:02,210 --> 00:53:03,950
Isn't it a surrender?

1330
00:53:04,080 --> 00:53:05,480
A document of surrender?

1331
00:53:05,480 --> 00:53:06,820
- Whatever. Geneva Conventions.
- Go for it.

1332
00:53:07,920 --> 00:53:09,190
End of war declaration.

1333
00:53:09,650 --> 00:53:12,120
We will go with
Japan's written oath of surrender.

1334
00:53:12,890 --> 00:53:13,990
That is correct.

1335
00:53:14,060 --> 00:53:15,160
Gosh, that's a relief.

1336
00:53:15,560 --> 00:53:16,900
Japanese Instrument of Surrender.

1337
00:53:17,660 --> 00:53:18,900
- Instrument of Surrender?
- Instrument of Surrender?

1338
00:53:18,900 --> 00:53:20,400
The word "surrender" has to be included.

1339
00:53:20,500 --> 00:53:22,070
That was to announce the end of the war.

1340
00:53:22,070 --> 00:53:23,740
It's different from surrendering.

1341
00:53:23,740 --> 00:53:25,670
Instrument of Surrender? That was it?

1342
00:53:27,270 --> 00:53:28,270
Let's go.

1343
00:53:29,510 --> 00:53:31,510
I feel like an airhead.

1344
00:53:31,510 --> 00:53:33,140
- Don't say that.
- The leaders of each group...

1345
00:53:33,140 --> 00:53:35,480
should head to the Community Center...

1346
00:53:35,580 --> 00:53:37,680
- to collect the resources won.
- Great work.

1347
00:53:37,680 --> 00:53:38,720
Great work.

1348
00:53:39,180 --> 00:53:41,190
- See you.
- I'll be back.

1349
00:53:41,790 --> 00:53:43,920
Please collect the resources produced...

1350
00:53:43,920 --> 00:53:45,320
by Team White.

1351
00:53:45,690 --> 00:53:47,830
- Please collect the resources produced...
- Thank you.

1352
00:53:47,830 --> 00:53:49,290
by Team Blue.

1353
00:53:49,830 --> 00:53:53,830
Team Red can select
the type of credit to produce.

1354
00:53:54,700 --> 00:53:58,700
(Team Red credit selection)

1355
00:53:59,370 --> 00:54:03,310
(Before production)

1356
00:54:03,880 --> 00:54:08,150
However, if Team Red chooses to produce
pollution-free credits...

1357
00:54:08,510 --> 00:54:09,810
What are pollution-free credits?

1358
00:54:10,480 --> 00:54:13,950
Two pollution-free credits are provided
with one correct answer.

1359
00:54:14,920 --> 00:54:16,590
There's environmental pollution.

1360
00:54:16,850 --> 00:54:19,720
The decision between regular credits
and pollution-free credits...

1361
00:54:19,820 --> 00:54:21,360
can be made at the Community Center...

1362
00:54:21,360 --> 00:54:24,230
when collecting the resources...

1363
00:54:24,230 --> 00:54:26,160
- after the production session is over.
- Let's answer the questions first.

1364
00:54:27,930 --> 00:54:31,570
If you select regular credits,
you get 3 credits for 1 question.

1365
00:54:31,800 --> 00:54:33,970
If you select pollution-free credits,

1366
00:54:34,310 --> 00:54:36,570
you get 2 credits for 1 question.

1367
00:54:36,570 --> 00:54:38,480
(Pollution-free credits have
a lower production efficiency.)

1368
00:54:38,880 --> 00:54:40,950
Whenever regular credits are used,

1369
00:54:41,350 --> 00:54:42,810
pollution occurs.

1370
00:54:44,150 --> 00:54:47,850
The pollution level goes up
when regular credits are used.

1371
00:54:48,290 --> 00:54:51,290
Pollution-free credits
do not cause pollution.

1372
00:54:52,160 --> 00:54:54,030
When the pollution level is high,

1373
00:54:54,860 --> 00:54:58,000
a huge damage might occur...

1374
00:54:58,460 --> 00:55:01,130
against the safety and assets
of the Community Town residents.

1375
00:55:05,570 --> 00:55:08,070
I thought this was great for us.

1376
00:55:08,210 --> 00:55:09,740
It's a new type of credit.

1377
00:55:10,310 --> 00:55:13,480
I didn't find much meaning
with the credits yesterday.

1378
00:55:13,710 --> 00:55:18,420
(Credits weren't seen
to be valuable yesterday.)

1379
00:55:18,580 --> 00:55:21,250
With pollution-free credits,

1380
00:55:21,490 --> 00:55:24,390
I believe we can change minds
and turn things around.

1381
00:55:25,290 --> 00:55:27,190
- If we use regular credits,
- Yes?

1382
00:55:27,530 --> 00:55:29,160
all of our assets...

1383
00:55:29,160 --> 00:55:31,200
can be harmed.

1384
00:55:31,360 --> 00:55:33,160
That means we should use
pollution-free credits.

1385
00:55:34,130 --> 00:55:37,170
But let's say
we used pollution-free credits...

1386
00:55:37,170 --> 00:55:39,170
- and did well to protect the environment.
- Right.

1387
00:55:39,340 --> 00:55:41,670
If the other teams cause pollution...

1388
00:55:41,670 --> 00:55:43,840
- Right. All of us will get harmed.
- Right.

1389
00:55:43,840 --> 00:55:47,380
I don't see the need to use
pollution-free credits if that's the case.

1390
00:55:48,250 --> 00:55:50,250
But this is what it's like.

1391
00:55:50,250 --> 00:55:52,520
If we start producing
pollution-free credits from now on,

1392
00:55:53,020 --> 00:55:56,450
we will be able to delay future harm
against our safety.

1393
00:55:58,820 --> 00:56:01,730
Should we go for pollution-free credits
since we've earned a lot?

1394
00:56:01,730 --> 00:56:02,860
That could be good.

1395
00:56:03,860 --> 00:56:06,160
We'll choose pollution-free credits.

1396
00:56:06,360 --> 00:56:08,730
You have chosen pollution-free credits.

1397
00:56:09,470 --> 00:56:13,240
Please collect the resources produced
by Team Red.

1398
00:56:13,500 --> 00:56:15,310
The pollution-free credits have holes.

1399
00:56:18,640 --> 00:56:20,880
There are holes in these credits.

1400
00:56:20,880 --> 00:56:22,510
(Resources After Day 2's Production)

1401
00:56:22,510 --> 00:56:23,920
(Team White:
90 diamonds, 10 lives, 6 credits)

1402
00:56:23,920 --> 00:56:25,280
(Team Blue: 60 diamonds, 21 lives,
5 credits)

1403
00:56:25,280 --> 00:56:26,980
(Team Red:
50 diamonds, 6 lives, 29 credits)

1404
00:56:27,550 --> 00:56:29,820
Would Black know
about the pollution level?

1405
00:56:32,560 --> 00:56:33,660
We got something.

1406
00:56:33,660 --> 00:56:35,160
There's something in the mailbox.

1407
00:56:35,290 --> 00:56:36,430
What?

1408
00:56:36,430 --> 00:56:37,860
(A new rule card arrives at the dorm.)

1409
00:56:37,860 --> 00:56:39,500
We got something. Awesome.

1410
00:56:39,500 --> 00:56:40,530
We got something.

1411
00:56:40,530 --> 00:56:41,900
- Shall we take a look?
- I'm scared.

1412
00:56:42,130 --> 00:56:45,170
- Gosh! I'm scared!
- Is it going to say Black got it right?

1413
00:56:47,040 --> 00:56:49,370
Couldn't it be a death sentence
from Black?

1414
00:56:49,510 --> 00:56:51,410
"Black has already figured it out."

1415
00:56:51,410 --> 00:56:53,010
"You must make a purchase."
What if it says things like that?

1416
00:56:53,010 --> 00:56:54,180
Gosh, what is this?

1417
00:56:55,210 --> 00:56:56,580
Rules of war?

1418
00:56:57,250 --> 00:56:59,350
- It's scary.
- War? What?

1419
00:56:59,820 --> 00:57:01,020
Rules of war?

1420
00:57:01,490 --> 00:57:03,190
Rules of war. Gosh!

1421
00:57:03,190 --> 00:57:06,360
- War?
- This is insane. Rules of war.

1422
00:57:06,560 --> 00:57:07,630
War?

1423
00:57:08,330 --> 00:57:10,400
Rules of war, all of a sudden?

1424
00:57:10,800 --> 00:57:12,960
Well, we can never be peaceful.

1425
00:57:13,200 --> 00:57:15,600
- War?
- It's war.

1426
00:57:15,600 --> 00:57:17,500
- I hate war.
- So do I.

1427
00:57:17,500 --> 00:57:20,410
- We won't be left alone.
- We must go to war.

1428
00:57:20,640 --> 00:57:23,070
Here are the rules of war.

1429
00:57:23,070 --> 00:57:24,340
(Rules of war)

1430
00:57:24,580 --> 00:57:26,410
- A group that fails to earn...
- "A group that fails to earn..."

1431
00:57:26,410 --> 00:57:28,250
- resources through trade...
- "resources through trade..."

1432
00:57:28,250 --> 00:57:30,050
- will be able to declare war.
- "will be able to declare war."

1433
00:57:32,450 --> 00:57:36,720
Another group is chosen to be taken
to the battlefield...

1434
00:57:36,720 --> 00:57:38,620
for a group battle.

1435
00:57:40,160 --> 00:57:44,260
The winning group will be able to earn...

1436
00:57:44,260 --> 00:57:46,230
half of all of
the losing group's resources.

1437
00:57:46,230 --> 00:57:47,530
- Really?
- Half of all of the resources?

1438
00:57:47,700 --> 00:57:48,900
- Half of all of the resources.
- Awesome.

1439
00:57:49,200 --> 00:57:50,640
We'll go to war if things don't work out.

1440
00:57:50,640 --> 00:57:52,100
- It's a true war.
- Right.

1441
00:57:52,100 --> 00:57:54,770
"Half of all of the resources?"

1442
00:57:56,040 --> 00:57:59,280
My stomach hurts right now.

1443
00:57:59,680 --> 00:58:02,610
I'm not lying. My stomach hurts.

1444
00:58:02,610 --> 00:58:04,120
Once we lose,

1445
00:58:04,120 --> 00:58:06,880
- Gosh! My stomach hurts!
- that's the end of us.

1446
00:58:08,220 --> 00:58:09,850
We're definitely going to go to war.

1447
00:58:09,850 --> 00:58:12,190
This is the start of survival.

1448
00:58:12,190 --> 00:58:14,130
It's an attempt to shake everyone up.

1449
00:58:14,130 --> 00:58:15,660
"This is bad."

1450
00:58:15,660 --> 00:58:18,130
The seed of fear
started to grow inside of everyone.

1451
00:58:18,560 --> 00:58:19,800
"A bolt out of the blue."

1452
00:58:20,630 --> 00:58:21,730
"I want to die."

1453
00:58:23,030 --> 00:58:24,100
"Stress."

1454
00:58:24,100 --> 00:58:26,500
"A sudden rush of pressure."

1455
00:58:26,900 --> 00:58:29,370
"This is exciting."

1456
00:58:29,870 --> 00:58:31,880
"We're going all in."

1457
00:58:31,880 --> 00:58:32,980
It was inevitable.

1458
00:58:33,140 --> 00:58:34,880
Once the rules of war were announced,

1459
00:58:34,880 --> 00:58:38,080
there will be something
that forces us to go to war.

1460
00:58:38,180 --> 00:58:40,920
I thought that we had to be
prepared for that.

1461
00:58:40,920 --> 00:58:42,720
When a group wishes to go to war,

1462
00:58:42,720 --> 00:58:46,320
the leader must visit the Community Center
during the trade activity session,

1463
00:58:46,320 --> 00:58:49,460
declare war, and pay the fee for war.

1464
00:58:50,830 --> 00:58:54,630
The fee for war will be announced
by the number of diamonds every day.

1465
00:58:54,630 --> 00:58:57,800
It will be deducted from
the total prize money...

1466
00:58:58,270 --> 00:59:00,370
based on the value of diamonds
of that day.

1467
00:59:01,210 --> 00:59:02,440
It's deducted from the prize money.

1468
00:59:02,910 --> 00:59:06,340
- It's from our own money.
- It's deducted.

1469
00:59:06,410 --> 00:59:09,480
If we go to war,
that will cut down the 200,000 dollars.

1470
00:59:09,480 --> 00:59:10,720
There are 200 diamonds.

1471
00:59:10,720 --> 00:59:12,620
Let's say the fee costs 20 diamonds.

1472
00:59:12,620 --> 00:59:14,590
That's 20,000 dollars, as it's a 10th.

1473
00:59:14,590 --> 00:59:16,390
That will cut down the prize money
to 180,000 dollars.

1474
00:59:16,390 --> 00:59:17,560
This is for Team White.

1475
00:59:18,290 --> 00:59:21,060
Right. They will surely target us.

1476
00:59:21,060 --> 00:59:22,090
Definitely.

1477
00:59:22,090 --> 00:59:24,660
A declaration of war cannot be canceled.

1478
00:59:25,060 --> 00:59:26,760
Once war is declared,

1479
00:59:26,760 --> 00:59:29,200
all trade activities will stop.

1480
00:59:29,200 --> 00:59:31,870
Community Town will enter a state of war.

1481
00:59:32,300 --> 00:59:34,540
It's inevitable once it gets declared.

1482
00:59:34,540 --> 00:59:36,070
- Right. It's war right away.
- Right.

1483
00:59:36,070 --> 00:59:37,140
It's a state of war right away.

1484
00:59:37,140 --> 00:59:38,210
This is harsh.

1485
00:59:38,210 --> 00:59:40,710
Before the announcement
to the battlefield is made,

1486
00:59:40,710 --> 00:59:44,020
the following war activities may proceed.

1487
00:59:44,680 --> 00:59:46,750
Number one, forming an alliance.

1488
00:59:47,020 --> 00:59:50,490
The group in battle
can form an alliance with another group.

1489
00:59:50,620 --> 00:59:54,260
The allied group can enter the battle.

1490
00:59:54,330 --> 00:59:58,130
The spoils of war are based
on the initial group of war,

1491
00:59:58,130 --> 00:59:59,830
but when there's an allied group,

1492
00:59:59,830 --> 01:00:03,400
the spoils can be shared
or paid off together.

1493
01:00:03,470 --> 01:00:06,540
However, Team Black cannot participate
in the war...

1494
01:00:06,540 --> 01:00:08,540
or form an alliance.

1495
01:00:08,540 --> 01:00:10,510
Will they share the risk as well?

1496
01:00:10,510 --> 01:00:11,710
Right. It must be like that.

1497
01:00:11,710 --> 01:00:13,480
- If White goes against us,
- White goes against us,

1498
01:00:13,480 --> 01:00:16,080
- and we must persuade Red.
- we must persuade Red.

1499
01:00:16,580 --> 01:00:20,590
The number of members might influence
the war.

1500
01:00:20,590 --> 01:00:23,150
Is it better to have more numbers?

1501
01:00:23,150 --> 01:00:25,790
The numbers will be the same
if they form an alliance.

1502
01:00:25,790 --> 01:00:28,560
- Number two, weapon purchase.
- There are weapons as well?

1503
01:00:28,560 --> 01:00:30,830
During a state of war,

1504
01:00:30,830 --> 01:00:32,860
you may purchase weapons
at the Community Center.

1505
01:00:33,460 --> 01:00:36,230
There are three types of weapons.

1506
01:00:36,230 --> 01:00:38,240
They differ in price
based on their grades.

1507
01:00:38,240 --> 01:00:40,140
They are stronger when higher in price.

1508
01:00:40,300 --> 01:00:43,270
There is one weapon in each grade,

1509
01:00:43,270 --> 01:00:45,940
and there is no purchase limit
for each group.

1510
01:00:45,940 --> 01:00:48,710
They have no risks in declaring war.

1511
01:00:48,710 --> 01:00:50,210
They can issue more anyway.

1512
01:00:50,210 --> 01:00:52,120
They will surely declare war.

1513
01:00:52,120 --> 01:00:55,420
When purchasing a weapon, it will get
deducted from the prize money...

1514
01:00:55,420 --> 01:00:57,590
based on the value of diamonds
of that day.

1515
01:00:57,820 --> 01:00:59,890
Why does it keep getting deducted?

1516
01:00:59,890 --> 01:01:02,230
This was from the Community Center.

1517
01:01:02,230 --> 01:01:03,960
This is a fun society.

1518
01:01:03,960 --> 01:01:04,960
War?

1519
01:01:10,870 --> 01:01:14,110
When lives become rare,

1520
01:01:14,410 --> 01:01:16,270
- war will be inevitable.
- Right.

1521
01:01:16,270 --> 01:01:18,380
It's a matter of us surviving
or them surviving.

1522
01:01:18,380 --> 01:01:20,240
- Right. We must go after each other.
- Right.

1523
01:01:20,480 --> 01:01:25,420
- When we fail to secure six lives,
- Right.

1524
01:01:25,420 --> 01:01:27,120
we have to go to war.

1525
01:01:30,150 --> 01:01:32,760
- That becomes the leverage for war.
- Right.

1526
01:01:32,890 --> 01:01:35,460
We have to go to war
or give up on someone.

1527
01:01:35,460 --> 01:01:36,790
- We have to give up on one member.
- Right.

1528
01:01:36,790 --> 01:01:37,960
It's a bet.

1529
01:01:38,300 --> 01:01:39,860
We were the villains.

1530
01:01:39,860 --> 01:01:42,100
This is bad.
We said Team White was the villain.

1531
01:01:42,100 --> 01:01:43,230
Why not go to war?

1532
01:01:43,500 --> 01:01:45,870
We'll all die if we don't survive.

1533
01:01:46,200 --> 01:01:47,570
That can't be helped.

1534
01:01:47,770 --> 01:01:49,340
We could hold hands
and head home together.

1535
01:01:49,340 --> 01:01:50,740
Right. We'll all die.

1536
01:01:52,240 --> 01:01:54,550
They must want us to have fewer members.

1537
01:01:54,810 --> 01:01:56,450
- They'll think that way.
- Right.

1538
01:01:56,450 --> 01:01:58,950
- Right.
- The six of us surviving...

1539
01:01:58,950 --> 01:02:00,420
only benefits us.

1540
01:02:00,420 --> 01:02:02,450
- This is bad.
- It won't benefit them at all.

1541
01:02:02,690 --> 01:02:03,820
"The six of us must survive..."

1542
01:02:03,820 --> 01:02:05,390
"before we kill you first."

1543
01:02:06,420 --> 01:02:08,030
- We'll end up saying that.
- Right.

1544
01:02:08,030 --> 01:02:09,930
"If we don't secure our lives,"

1545
01:02:09,930 --> 01:02:12,130
- "we'll go to war."
- Right.

1546
01:02:12,130 --> 01:02:13,930
"It's more exciting
when we fight as a group of six."

1547
01:02:16,730 --> 01:02:20,000
The ones who kept going on about peace
until this morning...

1548
01:02:20,440 --> 01:02:22,170
changed after hearing about war.

1549
01:02:22,170 --> 01:02:23,310
"We should go to war!"

1550
01:02:23,470 --> 01:02:26,310
Luna looked excited.

1551
01:02:26,310 --> 01:02:27,340
She's already at the top.

1552
01:02:27,340 --> 01:02:29,250
"Just burn our money."

1553
01:02:29,250 --> 01:02:33,380
Saying those things with a smile
felt scary.

1554
01:02:33,820 --> 01:02:35,590
This is what's scary about people.

1555
01:02:35,590 --> 01:02:38,660
As soon as those rules were announced,

1556
01:02:38,690 --> 01:02:41,260
we went, "Sure. Let's battle it out
if things don't work out."

1557
01:02:41,560 --> 01:02:44,800
Seeing us say that naturally...

1558
01:02:45,230 --> 01:02:47,160
gave me goosebumps.

1559
01:02:47,570 --> 01:02:50,230
It's better to fight
if we are short on lives.

1560
01:02:50,430 --> 01:02:51,740
We'll get eliminated anyway.

1561
01:02:52,000 --> 01:02:54,340
I expected that moment to come.

1562
01:02:54,340 --> 01:02:56,810
But that has to be delayed
as much as possible.

1563
01:02:56,810 --> 01:02:58,780
The most important part is the fee of war.

1564
01:02:59,140 --> 01:03:00,850
I expect it to be really expensive.

1565
01:03:00,850 --> 01:03:04,550
I believe it will become
more expensive over time.

1566
01:03:04,550 --> 01:03:06,720
Once it starts,

1567
01:03:06,720 --> 01:03:09,090
war will be inevitable.

1568
01:03:09,220 --> 01:03:11,620
The sound of the first gunshots...

1569
01:03:11,620 --> 01:03:13,960
must be delayed as much as possible
for the best of all of us.

1570
01:03:14,290 --> 01:03:16,560
War will break out, no matter what.

1571
01:03:16,560 --> 01:03:19,130
But I don't plan to make it happen soon.

1572
01:03:19,130 --> 01:03:21,200
War causes harm anyway.

1573
01:03:21,400 --> 01:03:24,400
But when that moment comes,

1574
01:03:24,400 --> 01:03:26,100
we can be the ones to pull the trigger.

1575
01:03:26,340 --> 01:03:28,170
If it's going to happen anyway,

1576
01:03:28,170 --> 01:03:29,810
we have a higher chance...

1577
01:03:29,810 --> 01:03:32,080
of being at an advantage.

1578
01:03:32,240 --> 01:03:34,810
That will bring up
our chance of winning as well.

1579
01:03:34,810 --> 01:03:36,610
This was my calculation.

1580
01:03:37,410 --> 01:03:40,280
Don't threaten Team White too much.

1581
01:03:40,350 --> 01:03:41,550
They have a lot of diamonds...

1582
01:03:41,550 --> 01:03:43,720
and they can purchase weapons
and declare war.

1583
01:03:43,990 --> 01:03:45,660
"If you don't give us lives,"

1584
01:03:45,660 --> 01:03:47,890
"we have no choice but to declare war."

1585
01:03:48,060 --> 01:03:50,830
It's easier for them to declare war.

1586
01:03:50,830 --> 01:03:52,800
Right. War is easier for them.

1587
01:03:52,800 --> 01:03:54,330
They have the money and numbers.

1588
01:03:54,700 --> 01:03:56,030
They're thugs.

1589
01:03:57,270 --> 01:03:59,370
This team, Team Blue, is in danger...

1590
01:03:59,370 --> 01:04:01,570
because they have the lives.

1591
01:04:01,570 --> 01:04:03,010
If Team Blue doesn't sell the lives,

1592
01:04:03,010 --> 01:04:05,910
- If they don't sell them...
- we will ally with Team White.

1593
01:04:05,910 --> 01:04:07,280
- Right.
- "Let's wipe out Team Blue."

1594
01:04:07,280 --> 01:04:09,080
If we go, "Let's wipe them out..."

1595
01:04:09,380 --> 01:04:12,350
This is a rule for Team White.

1596
01:04:12,350 --> 01:04:16,090
Money and numbers are needed for war.

1597
01:04:16,090 --> 01:04:19,360
Team Blue always acted high-handedly...

1598
01:04:19,360 --> 01:04:20,560
as they knew they were
in a dominant position.

1599
01:04:20,560 --> 01:04:24,460
They acted like that
to bring out better deals.

1600
01:04:24,460 --> 01:04:27,160
But that kind of behavior
can be punished now.

1601
01:04:27,160 --> 01:04:29,730
That can be a spark of war.

1602
01:04:31,040 --> 01:04:32,540
Finally,

1603
01:04:33,100 --> 01:04:36,940
there was a way to stop
Team Blue's threats with their lives.

1604
01:04:37,240 --> 01:04:43,150
If Team Blue continues to
keep the lives to themselves,

1605
01:04:43,150 --> 01:04:45,880
there's a great way to threaten them.

1606
01:04:46,080 --> 01:04:47,690
I believe this is great for us.

1607
01:04:48,820 --> 01:04:52,360
Team Blue will end up becoming
the opponents.

1608
01:04:52,520 --> 01:04:53,590
Right.

1609
01:04:53,590 --> 01:04:55,890
Will half of what they have be taken?

1610
01:04:55,890 --> 01:04:56,990
Right.

1611
01:04:57,060 --> 01:04:58,130
That's crazy.

1612
01:04:58,260 --> 01:05:01,130
- Right.
- It's a revolution if we win today.

1613
01:05:01,130 --> 01:05:02,130
That's 11 lives.

1614
01:05:02,530 --> 01:05:04,570
That means we would be able to survive
until the end.

1615
01:05:05,040 --> 01:05:06,840
That's why war sounds like a good idea.

1616
01:05:07,940 --> 01:05:10,670
It's important to have
a good cause for war.

1617
01:05:10,670 --> 01:05:12,580
- If we start a war without a cause,
- Right.

1618
01:05:12,580 --> 01:05:14,650
they will definitely form an alliance.

1619
01:05:14,710 --> 01:05:17,780
If they ally with Team White,
we have no chance of winning.

1620
01:05:17,780 --> 01:05:19,350
What if we are to persuade Team White?

1621
01:05:19,550 --> 01:05:21,290
"We'll give you all of our credits."

1622
01:05:21,950 --> 01:05:24,390
- No. We need lives.
- Right.

1623
01:05:24,390 --> 01:05:26,160
We have to ally with them
because of their lives.

1624
01:05:26,690 --> 01:05:30,360
We should ask about
how many they are willing to trade off.

1625
01:05:30,460 --> 01:05:31,560
"How many do you want?"

1626
01:05:31,560 --> 01:05:32,900
"How many can you sell?"

1627
01:05:33,030 --> 01:05:34,100
"We won't sell any."

1628
01:05:34,100 --> 01:05:36,430
"Really? Then, we go to war."

1629
01:05:40,570 --> 01:05:41,740
But...

1630
01:05:41,870 --> 01:05:44,010
I'm not sure. This might be because
I'm a pacifist.

1631
01:05:44,010 --> 01:05:45,810
War must not break out.

1632
01:05:45,880 --> 01:05:47,210
If war breaks out,

1633
01:05:47,510 --> 01:05:50,180
our prize money gets deducted.

1634
01:05:52,250 --> 01:05:54,520
- That's what it's like in real life.
- Right.

1635
01:05:54,520 --> 01:05:57,920
Except for the benefit
of the ones who start war,

1636
01:05:57,920 --> 01:06:00,120
it's a constant destruction...

1637
01:06:00,120 --> 01:06:01,330
of everything else.

1638
01:06:05,260 --> 01:06:06,930
This is a red flag for us.

1639
01:06:07,460 --> 01:06:11,400
But if Team White doesn't want to
go to war,

1640
01:06:11,400 --> 01:06:13,970
they would want 6 lives.
We can't give out 6 lives.

1641
01:06:18,480 --> 01:06:22,580
We're stacked with lives right now.

1642
01:06:23,280 --> 01:06:27,950
If we threaten the ones
with their survival,

1643
01:06:28,190 --> 01:06:31,090
- they will start a war.
- They will start a war.

1644
01:06:31,090 --> 01:06:35,030
"If you care only about your safety,"

1645
01:06:35,030 --> 01:06:38,100
"the ones who are fighting to survive
will bite."

1646
01:06:38,360 --> 01:06:42,430
The ones who are fighting to survive
always cause a revolt.

1647
01:06:42,970 --> 01:06:45,570
They will start a war
if they are about to die.

1648
01:06:45,800 --> 01:06:46,840
Right.

1649
01:06:51,740 --> 01:06:53,580
But if we win...

1650
01:06:54,610 --> 01:06:55,980
That will be huge.

1651
01:06:55,980 --> 01:06:58,020
If we win,

1652
01:06:58,180 --> 01:07:00,380
we are...

1653
01:07:00,720 --> 01:07:03,050
- Shall we just...
- Gosh.

1654
01:07:03,050 --> 01:07:04,090
We might end up
starting a war at this rate.

1655
01:07:04,590 --> 01:07:05,860
We might end up
starting a war at this rate.

1656
01:07:05,960 --> 01:07:07,790
She's going to start a war.

1657
01:07:07,790 --> 01:07:09,030
"Let's start a war."

1658
01:07:09,030 --> 01:07:10,660
What if we win?

1659
01:07:11,200 --> 01:07:12,300
Right.

1660
01:07:12,300 --> 01:07:14,200
- Then it's totally...
- Right.

1661
01:07:15,470 --> 01:07:16,970
Then we can get it done
without lifting a finger.

1662
01:07:19,470 --> 01:07:20,470
Or...

1663
01:07:20,470 --> 01:07:22,670
- This is so stressful. It's crazy.
- Look.

1664
01:07:22,670 --> 01:07:25,110
We could contact the White first.

1665
01:07:25,110 --> 01:07:28,180
If this war is unavoidable,

1666
01:07:28,680 --> 01:07:31,850
and we must win,

1667
01:07:31,850 --> 01:07:33,250
how about we start it first?

1668
01:07:33,250 --> 01:07:36,050
Because we can definitely beat
nine people.

1669
01:07:37,420 --> 01:07:39,720
Think about it.
Then we can wipe off Team Credit.

1670
01:07:40,860 --> 01:07:41,860
You know what I mean?

1671
01:07:42,090 --> 01:07:43,560
If we wipe them off,

1672
01:07:43,560 --> 01:07:45,400
we get to keep what they have.

1673
01:07:45,400 --> 01:07:46,400
Those credits...

1674
01:07:46,400 --> 01:07:47,970
- The credits...
- We can split them.

1675
01:07:47,970 --> 01:07:51,870
That way, we can earn more lives
with those credits.

1676
01:07:52,270 --> 01:07:53,700
Now that I think about it,

1677
01:07:53,700 --> 01:07:55,210
if anyone comes after us,

1678
01:07:55,210 --> 01:07:58,740
there aren't many people left
to earn lives.

1679
01:07:59,210 --> 01:08:00,680
We can take advantage of it.

1680
01:08:00,680 --> 01:08:01,910
We might as well...

1681
01:08:01,910 --> 01:08:03,510
attack them first.

1682
01:08:03,510 --> 01:08:06,120
We have to attack them once, at least.

1683
01:08:06,120 --> 01:08:07,850
We have to declare war, at least once.
It's unavoidable.

1684
01:08:07,850 --> 01:08:10,020
We can't help it due to the system.

1685
01:08:10,020 --> 01:08:11,590
We have to make an ally,

1686
01:08:11,590 --> 01:08:14,190
but if we form an alliance with them,
it's our loss.

1687
01:08:14,190 --> 01:08:15,690
So we might as well go talk to them first,

1688
01:08:15,690 --> 01:08:17,060
form an alliance,

1689
01:08:17,060 --> 01:08:18,700
and kill them all.

1690
01:08:19,230 --> 01:08:20,330
- Then...
- I like that.

1691
01:08:20,330 --> 01:08:24,230
the chance of us losing the war
is unlikely.

1692
01:08:24,230 --> 01:08:25,870
We get to earn more credits...

1693
01:08:25,870 --> 01:08:27,570
to buy lives,

1694
01:08:27,570 --> 01:08:28,910
and we can all survive.

1695
01:08:28,910 --> 01:08:31,440
We should persuade them
and form an alliance.

1696
01:08:32,510 --> 01:08:34,280
That is our only option. Look.

1697
01:08:34,280 --> 01:08:36,350
We have to get into action.

1698
01:08:36,350 --> 01:08:38,320
I didn't realize that we were cornered.

1699
01:08:38,320 --> 01:08:40,020
I thought we were safe after today,

1700
01:08:40,020 --> 01:08:41,550
but we're not.

1701
01:08:41,550 --> 01:08:42,990
This can't wait.

1702
01:08:42,990 --> 01:08:44,860
We have to get this done before today.

1703
01:08:44,860 --> 01:08:47,060
We have to declare war even tomorrow.

1704
01:08:47,560 --> 01:08:48,890
She's different from yesterday.

1705
01:08:48,890 --> 01:08:50,530
She's a different person today.

1706
01:08:50,530 --> 01:08:52,560
- Did she change while sleeping?
- She seems possessed.

1707
01:08:52,560 --> 01:08:54,470
What do you think?
You know what I mean, right?

1708
01:08:54,470 --> 01:08:56,570
We need to contact them as soon as we can.

1709
01:08:56,570 --> 01:08:57,870
- Yes.
- It's all about timing.

1710
01:08:57,870 --> 01:08:59,140
We have to do it as soon as we can.

1711
01:08:59,140 --> 01:09:00,540
If I got this right,

1712
01:09:00,540 --> 01:09:01,840
do you want to declare war today?

1713
01:09:02,040 --> 01:09:03,110
- No.
- No.

1714
01:09:03,110 --> 01:09:04,240
We have to talk to them today...

1715
01:09:04,240 --> 01:09:05,440
- and declare war tomorrow.
- She wants to...

1716
01:09:05,710 --> 01:09:07,310
win Team White over today...

1717
01:09:07,310 --> 01:09:09,550
and declare war tomorrow.

1718
01:09:09,810 --> 01:09:12,950
I think this is a very good idea.

1719
01:09:12,950 --> 01:09:14,720
But we need to think...

1720
01:09:14,720 --> 01:09:17,490
if getting rid of Team Red...

1721
01:09:17,490 --> 01:09:19,890
will only benefit us.

1722
01:09:19,890 --> 01:09:21,930
Of course not.

1723
01:09:22,230 --> 01:09:25,630
But if we agree...

1724
01:09:25,630 --> 01:09:27,430
not to declare war in the end,

1725
01:09:27,430 --> 01:09:29,800
then it works for us.

1726
01:09:30,530 --> 01:09:33,440
But that's not the case,
and we should prepare for that.

1727
01:09:36,010 --> 01:09:38,980
- This is so tough.
- We're talking about it even now.

1728
01:09:39,480 --> 01:09:41,710
We're worried about the team splitting up.

1729
01:09:41,710 --> 01:09:45,050
- Of course.
- The chance of us...

1730
01:09:45,280 --> 01:09:48,850
becoming a majority is
either now or never.

1731
01:09:51,820 --> 01:09:54,320
Still, we can keep the team safe this way.

1732
01:09:56,190 --> 01:09:58,200
Because this wipes out one team.

1733
01:09:58,460 --> 01:10:00,630
And the total number of lives we have...

1734
01:10:00,630 --> 01:10:02,370
can save nine people.

1735
01:10:02,970 --> 01:10:05,000
So if we team up with them,

1736
01:10:05,000 --> 01:10:07,100
we gain peace.

1737
01:10:07,100 --> 01:10:08,210
And that's done through a war.

1738
01:10:09,570 --> 01:10:12,180
In the end, a war is necessary
for our peace.

1739
01:10:17,650 --> 01:10:20,250
In the end, doing it today...

1740
01:10:20,550 --> 01:10:24,150
will get us allies at the lowest cost,

1741
01:10:24,490 --> 01:10:27,590
and it's the fastest way to gain peace.

1742
01:10:29,560 --> 01:10:30,560
Gosh.

1743
01:10:32,200 --> 01:10:35,570
In my opinion, I think we have...

1744
01:10:35,570 --> 01:10:39,040
enough number of lives.

1745
01:10:39,240 --> 01:10:40,600
I think...

1746
01:10:41,210 --> 01:10:45,140
it's enough to survive for four days.

1747
01:10:45,140 --> 01:10:47,410
We could increase the time...

1748
01:10:47,680 --> 01:10:49,750
to play the game together.

1749
01:10:49,750 --> 01:10:53,220
It's not just for them,

1750
01:10:53,220 --> 01:10:55,220
but I believe there's a gain...

1751
01:10:55,220 --> 01:10:58,490
from keeping society running.

1752
01:10:58,490 --> 01:11:02,030
But they're saying
we must secure what we have,

1753
01:11:02,030 --> 01:11:05,730
and that we must declare war.

1754
01:11:06,200 --> 01:11:08,730
We have completely different opinions,

1755
01:11:08,730 --> 01:11:11,300
so I don't even know...

1756
01:11:12,070 --> 01:11:13,540
where to start.

1757
01:11:13,540 --> 01:11:15,010
If I were to bring it up,

1758
01:11:15,010 --> 01:11:17,510
I don't know how to persuade them.

1759
01:11:17,810 --> 01:11:19,110
If there are three people,

1760
01:11:19,510 --> 01:11:22,450
it's split into 2 to 1.

1761
01:11:22,650 --> 01:11:25,120
And it seems I'm the one.

1762
01:11:25,120 --> 01:11:26,550
Because I'm a minority,

1763
01:11:26,550 --> 01:11:29,890
I was losing confidence in myself.

1764
01:11:30,290 --> 01:11:32,090
Maybe they're right.

1765
01:11:32,560 --> 01:11:34,560
I had a hard time...

1766
01:11:34,560 --> 01:11:38,130
because that didn't sound absurd.

1767
01:11:38,130 --> 01:11:40,100
To persuade them,

1768
01:11:40,100 --> 01:11:43,470
I needed to say something that excels
their ideas.

1769
01:11:43,470 --> 01:11:45,040
But it didn't work at all.

1770
01:11:45,540 --> 01:11:46,800
They wouldn't listen.

1771
01:11:47,640 --> 01:11:50,470
Is individual ability all we're taking
with us...

1772
01:11:51,110 --> 01:11:54,010
from this survival?

1773
01:11:54,280 --> 01:11:56,880
That thought kept occurring to me...

1774
01:11:56,880 --> 01:11:58,580
and made me dizzy.

1775
01:11:58,580 --> 01:12:00,580
(Writer Salt)

1776
01:12:00,580 --> 01:12:01,590
So...

1777
01:12:05,520 --> 01:12:08,060
I know it's funny. It's only a game.

1778
01:12:12,260 --> 01:12:13,630
So I'm...

1779
01:12:15,000 --> 01:12:17,230
I'm flustered right now...

1780
01:12:17,500 --> 01:12:18,600
by the fact that I'm crying.

1781
01:12:27,710 --> 01:12:30,380
From now on, you can use the supermarket.

1782
01:12:30,380 --> 01:12:31,650
Do you want to go to
the supermarket together?

1783
01:12:31,650 --> 01:12:32,780
- Sounds good.
- Sure.

1784
01:12:33,380 --> 01:12:34,890
I'm curious about the price range.

1785
01:12:34,890 --> 01:12:36,150
Me too. I'm hungry.

1786
01:12:36,320 --> 01:12:37,990
What's Team Black's strategy?

1787
01:12:39,360 --> 01:12:40,920
- They're away.
- They're away.

1788
01:12:40,920 --> 01:12:43,060
Vector is planning on something.

1789
01:12:43,060 --> 01:12:44,230
Now is the time.

1790
01:12:44,230 --> 01:12:46,330
- It's Vector.
- Hello.

1791
01:12:46,330 --> 01:12:47,700
It's open as soon as we're here.

1792
01:12:47,700 --> 01:12:49,000
Hi, Vector.

1793
01:12:49,000 --> 01:12:50,430
Hello.

1794
01:12:50,430 --> 01:12:52,740
How did your productive activities
go today?

1795
01:12:52,740 --> 01:12:55,410
- Productive activities? Not bad.
- Not bad?

1796
01:12:55,410 --> 01:12:57,110
You look like you're in a good mood.

1797
01:12:57,110 --> 01:12:58,780
I'm very happy.

1798
01:12:58,780 --> 01:12:59,780
- Really?
- Yes.

1799
01:12:59,780 --> 01:13:01,010
Did you get to do
any productive activities?

1800
01:13:01,010 --> 01:13:02,050
You got it.

1801
01:13:02,750 --> 01:13:05,220
What kind of productive activities
did you do?

1802
01:13:05,220 --> 01:13:07,380
I need to produce these supplies.

1803
01:13:08,420 --> 01:13:10,750
To add popular items,

1804
01:13:10,750 --> 01:13:12,860
I have to answer the questions.

1805
01:13:12,860 --> 01:13:14,220
Do you get physical rewards...

1806
01:13:14,220 --> 01:13:15,260
- for productive activities?
- That's right.

1807
01:13:15,260 --> 01:13:18,160
I have pork belly and Coke Zero.

1808
01:13:18,160 --> 01:13:19,960
If you want a lunchbox,
you can have a lunchbox.

1809
01:13:19,960 --> 01:13:22,000
What do you want for lunch?

1810
01:13:22,000 --> 01:13:24,230
- Well...
- I want something with rice.

1811
01:13:24,230 --> 01:13:26,870
Have you heard about the war?

1812
01:13:26,870 --> 01:13:27,870
- Yes.
- Yes.

1813
01:13:28,410 --> 01:13:31,910
You have to pay for all war supplies
with diamonds.

1814
01:13:31,910 --> 01:13:34,380
You'll be like the US.

1815
01:13:34,780 --> 01:13:36,280
We're not going to have a war.

1816
01:13:36,810 --> 01:13:39,220
I want to avoid a war...

1817
01:13:39,220 --> 01:13:41,590
- because a war means someone has to die.
- Right.

1818
01:13:41,590 --> 01:13:45,260
That means less share for me.

1819
01:13:45,660 --> 01:13:47,390
Why is it less?

1820
01:13:47,390 --> 01:13:49,060
Because there are fewer people eating.

1821
01:13:49,060 --> 01:13:50,960
It means less food consumption.

1822
01:13:50,960 --> 01:13:54,730
One of the things I wanted to
tell your team was,

1823
01:13:55,270 --> 01:13:58,640
to raise the value of your diamonds,

1824
01:13:59,300 --> 01:14:00,940
you need inflation.

1825
01:14:01,300 --> 01:14:03,510
I need to make the products expensive...

1826
01:14:03,510 --> 01:14:05,380
for people to want more diamonds.

1827
01:14:07,540 --> 01:14:09,480
There's nothing I can do
about the war cost...

1828
01:14:09,480 --> 01:14:10,610
because that's not my authority.

1829
01:14:10,610 --> 01:14:14,180
But I can change the price of the food.

1830
01:14:14,180 --> 01:14:16,550
In the end, they'll have to buy
at least one egg.

1831
01:14:17,190 --> 01:14:18,560
That will put you...

1832
01:14:18,960 --> 01:14:21,530
in a favorable position
during the negotiations.

1833
01:14:21,530 --> 01:14:24,830
We can't help but create inflation.

1834
01:14:24,830 --> 01:14:26,500
- Right.
- But the thing is,

1835
01:14:26,500 --> 01:14:31,000
we'd like to set the limit with you.

1836
01:14:31,000 --> 01:14:32,900
- In the end, it's all related.
- Right.

1837
01:14:32,900 --> 01:14:35,140
What I can tell you is,
without issuing the diamonds,

1838
01:14:35,540 --> 01:14:36,810
I'll pretend they've been issued...

1839
01:14:38,210 --> 01:14:40,010
and raise the price.

1840
01:14:40,010 --> 01:14:41,380
Are you saying we should fix the price?

1841
01:14:41,810 --> 01:14:44,550
Then it becomes intimidation.

1842
01:14:44,550 --> 01:14:45,820
We can get...

1843
01:14:45,820 --> 01:14:48,290
lives and credits for a low price...

1844
01:14:48,290 --> 01:14:51,350
by intimidating them.

1845
01:14:51,590 --> 01:14:53,320
It'd be great if it went as you planned.

1846
01:14:53,320 --> 01:14:55,060
But I'm afraid it might backfire.

1847
01:14:55,060 --> 01:14:56,730
- Like starting a war?
- Yes. What if they fight back...

1848
01:14:56,730 --> 01:14:59,000
or start a war to steal them?

1849
01:14:59,000 --> 01:15:00,460
Or they might go,
"We're not trading anymore."

1850
01:15:00,460 --> 01:15:03,200
If they boycott trading for a day or two,

1851
01:15:03,200 --> 01:15:04,840
we actually...

1852
01:15:04,840 --> 01:15:06,770
- We'll lose a lot of lives.
- need...

1853
01:15:07,100 --> 01:15:09,440
a lot of lives.

1854
01:15:09,440 --> 01:15:11,170
We can't face a hostile phase...

1855
01:15:11,170 --> 01:15:13,480
for a long time.

1856
01:15:13,680 --> 01:15:16,580
I wonder if that's a good idea
from the start.

1857
01:15:16,580 --> 01:15:17,750
Right.

1858
01:15:18,450 --> 01:15:23,050
Vector said,
"I'm destined to cooperate with you..."

1859
01:15:23,050 --> 01:15:24,720
"because if you control the money supply,"

1860
01:15:24,720 --> 01:15:27,290
"it affects the price of my items."

1861
01:15:27,290 --> 01:15:29,330
He said things like that.

1862
01:15:29,330 --> 01:15:31,090
To be honest,

1863
01:15:31,090 --> 01:15:34,160
the money supply is pointless for Vector.

1864
01:15:34,830 --> 01:15:37,170
He has the power to set the price.

1865
01:15:37,170 --> 01:15:41,040
He's not that affected by us.

1866
01:15:41,140 --> 01:15:43,010
Yet, he keeps saying...

1867
01:15:43,010 --> 01:15:45,880
he wants to cooperate with us.

1868
01:15:46,480 --> 01:15:49,380
I think he is...

1869
01:15:49,810 --> 01:15:51,680
an extraordinary man.

1870
01:15:51,680 --> 01:15:55,190
Anyway, he's well aware
of Team Black's money supply.

1871
01:15:55,190 --> 01:15:56,750
So we need to...

1872
01:15:57,820 --> 01:16:00,090
He's not an ordinary man,
but we still need to...

1873
01:16:00,720 --> 01:16:02,030
talk to him into it.

1874
01:16:02,290 --> 01:16:06,060
Our plan is to build trust at first.

1875
01:16:06,300 --> 01:16:07,530
Team Red is coming.

1876
01:16:08,130 --> 01:16:10,100
- But it's...
- Hello.

1877
01:16:10,100 --> 01:16:11,700
- Hello.
- Hello.

1878
01:16:11,700 --> 01:16:13,100
Is the store not open yet?

1879
01:16:13,100 --> 01:16:15,140
- It's open.
- It's open. Do you need anything?

1880
01:16:15,370 --> 01:16:17,740
- I'm not sure. Donkey's starving.
- Well...

1881
01:16:17,740 --> 01:16:19,940
- Let's take a look.
- We need to eat.

1882
01:16:19,940 --> 01:16:21,650
- Let's go.
- He's getting dizzy.

1883
01:16:21,650 --> 01:16:22,880
- It's closing.
- Here...

1884
01:16:23,310 --> 01:16:24,950
Do you have the price ready?

1885
01:16:24,950 --> 01:16:26,020
Not yet.

1886
01:16:26,020 --> 01:16:27,880
Today was too... One second.

1887
01:16:27,880 --> 01:16:29,750
Let me check the money supply.

1888
01:16:29,750 --> 01:16:30,750
Okay.

1889
01:16:32,190 --> 01:16:34,320
If Team White says...

1890
01:16:34,820 --> 01:16:36,960
- they need the credits...
- Be generous?

1891
01:16:37,090 --> 01:16:40,860
- Let's keep it cool.
- Okay.

1892
01:16:40,860 --> 01:16:42,700
Even if there's no benefit to us,

1893
01:16:42,700 --> 01:16:44,270
we should give them enough...

1894
01:16:44,570 --> 01:16:46,100
and ask them to support us...

1895
01:16:46,100 --> 01:16:47,940
if a war is declared.

1896
01:16:48,740 --> 01:16:50,270
But if they betray us,

1897
01:16:50,510 --> 01:16:52,580
- then...
- Right. We can't do that on credit.

1898
01:16:52,580 --> 01:16:54,040
we'll just blow up the bombs.

1899
01:16:54,410 --> 01:16:56,650
Then let's kill them all.

1900
01:16:58,820 --> 01:16:59,820
With our skills.

1901
01:17:00,480 --> 01:17:01,480
Wonderful.

1902
01:17:01,480 --> 01:17:02,490
What are they going to do about it?

1903
01:17:05,990 --> 01:17:07,220
How did the game go today?

1904
01:17:07,490 --> 01:17:08,960
- It was harder than expected.
- Hard?

1905
01:17:08,960 --> 01:17:10,790
I could tell.

1906
01:17:10,790 --> 01:17:12,260
We thought it was over faster
than expected.

1907
01:17:12,260 --> 01:17:13,300
- Really?
- Yes.

1908
01:17:13,300 --> 01:17:14,660
- You saw the war, right?
- Yes.

1909
01:17:15,700 --> 01:17:16,830
Let's keep it peaceful...

1910
01:17:16,830 --> 01:17:18,500
It's too complicated.

1911
01:17:18,500 --> 01:17:19,540
Let's not fight.

1912
01:17:19,540 --> 01:17:22,410
If you don't give us lives,
we have no choice but to declare war.

1913
01:17:23,110 --> 01:17:25,410
It's all about life in the end, right?

1914
01:17:25,410 --> 01:17:27,680
- Yes.
- Because the lives are limited.

1915
01:17:27,680 --> 01:17:30,650
We have the same goal then.

1916
01:17:30,650 --> 01:17:31,980
To win lives.

1917
01:17:31,980 --> 01:17:32,980
That's true.

1918
01:17:32,980 --> 01:17:34,080
- You're right.
- Yes.

1919
01:17:35,720 --> 01:17:38,020
This is getting complicated.

1920
01:17:39,290 --> 01:17:41,120
- Then we will...
- We'll take six lunchboxes...

1921
01:17:41,790 --> 01:17:42,990
for this much.

1922
01:17:43,590 --> 01:17:45,130
- Five in total?
- Five in total.

1923
01:17:46,460 --> 01:17:49,500
So one diamond per lunchbox?

1924
01:17:49,930 --> 01:17:53,170
Because 1 diamond equals to 1,000 dollars.

1925
01:17:53,440 --> 01:17:54,670
- Then here's what we'll do.
- Okay.

1926
01:17:55,340 --> 01:17:57,010
One diamond per lunchbox.

1927
01:17:57,010 --> 01:17:58,710
- One diamond per lunchbox?
- Yes.

1928
01:17:59,040 --> 01:18:01,880
For 6 ramyeon and 6 sodas,

1929
01:18:01,880 --> 01:18:03,350
give me 4 more, so 10 in total.

1930
01:18:04,510 --> 01:18:07,220
You can have it for breakfast tomorrow
or in the middle of the night.

1931
01:18:07,420 --> 01:18:08,620
We don't eat in the middle of the night.

1932
01:18:08,620 --> 01:18:10,820
- We don't do that. We're on a diet.
- We don't eat breakfast.

1933
01:18:10,820 --> 01:18:12,490
But I want ten diamonds.

1934
01:18:12,490 --> 01:18:16,660
But we don't need to stock up
on food right now.

1935
01:18:16,660 --> 01:18:18,460
And we're Team White.

1936
01:18:19,730 --> 01:18:21,100
And the number of diamonds...

1937
01:18:21,100 --> 01:18:24,430
doesn't really matter to you...

1938
01:18:24,430 --> 01:18:25,670
- Of course.
- right now.

1939
01:18:25,670 --> 01:18:27,370
It only matters...

1940
01:18:27,370 --> 01:18:28,910
when the currency value is adjusted.

1941
01:18:28,910 --> 01:18:30,440
Even this afternoon,

1942
01:18:30,640 --> 01:18:32,510
if we adjust it...

1943
01:18:32,580 --> 01:18:34,240
But you never know.

1944
01:18:34,510 --> 01:18:36,780
Anyway, all we need is six lunchboxes.

1945
01:18:37,050 --> 01:18:38,350
- You only want to eat six lunchboxes?
- We don't need...

1946
01:18:38,350 --> 01:18:40,320
Yes. We don't need any more negotiations.

1947
01:18:40,650 --> 01:18:41,990
Okay. Wait until tomorrow.

1948
01:18:41,990 --> 01:18:43,950
You never know
how things will change tomorrow.

1949
01:18:43,950 --> 01:18:45,920
- Enjoy your lunchboxes for today.
- Okay.

1950
01:18:46,020 --> 01:18:47,120
Make your payment.

1951
01:18:47,360 --> 01:18:49,260
What a waste.

1952
01:18:49,260 --> 01:18:50,990
One, two, three,

1953
01:18:50,990 --> 01:18:53,330
four, five, six.

1954
01:18:53,330 --> 01:18:54,500
Thank you.

1955
01:18:54,500 --> 01:18:55,970
- Give us more.
- What?

1956
01:18:56,100 --> 01:18:57,800
- Maybe ramyeon?
- Give us 1 or 2 ramyeon.

1957
01:18:57,870 --> 01:18:59,040
Maybe like small cups?

1958
01:18:59,540 --> 01:19:01,910
- You have to buy it.
- You're nice.

1959
01:19:01,910 --> 01:19:04,810
We'll keep the price...

1960
01:19:04,840 --> 01:19:06,340
a secret.

1961
01:19:06,340 --> 01:19:09,080
You can charge other people more.

1962
01:19:09,180 --> 01:19:10,510
- Anyway,
- Thank you for the food.

1963
01:19:10,510 --> 01:19:11,680
thank you for making the first payment.

1964
01:19:11,680 --> 01:19:13,420
Let's keep a good relationship.

1965
01:19:13,920 --> 01:19:15,520
(Next is Team Red.)

1966
01:19:15,520 --> 01:19:17,020
Does the price vary?

1967
01:19:17,020 --> 01:19:19,490
Yes. What would you like to buy?

1968
01:19:19,620 --> 01:19:21,090
Tell us the price for ramyeon.

1969
01:19:21,860 --> 01:19:23,430
I'll have one big Yukgaejang.

1970
01:19:23,430 --> 01:19:25,300
Why don't you get one lunchbox each?

1971
01:19:25,300 --> 01:19:26,330
Okay.

1972
01:19:26,360 --> 01:19:28,330
I didn't give them anything on the house,

1973
01:19:28,630 --> 01:19:31,740
but if you can keep it a secret
since you're men,

1974
01:19:31,740 --> 01:19:33,240
I'll give you one ramyeon each for free.

1975
01:19:33,570 --> 01:19:35,370
Are you buying this too?

1976
01:19:35,370 --> 01:19:36,470
- We'll get that too.
- Yes.

1977
01:19:36,470 --> 01:19:38,540
- We can eat that later.
- Okay.

1978
01:19:38,640 --> 01:19:40,140
Including those three...

1979
01:19:40,180 --> 01:19:42,610
You can take two eggs.

1980
01:19:42,810 --> 01:19:44,210
Two diamonds for that.

1981
01:19:44,210 --> 01:19:45,780
- So five in total?
- Yes.

1982
01:19:46,480 --> 01:19:47,880
- Are you okay with that?
- Yes.

1983
01:19:47,980 --> 01:19:49,250
- Five.
- If you could do that for us...

1984
01:19:49,250 --> 01:19:50,320
Thank you.

1985
01:19:50,520 --> 01:19:53,120
The use of diamonds finally feels real.

1986
01:19:53,490 --> 01:19:55,630
- Don't tell anyone about the price.
- Okay.

1987
01:19:55,760 --> 01:19:56,960
(Team Red's purchase with 5 diamonds)

1988
01:19:56,960 --> 01:19:58,600
- Thank you.
- Team White's order...

1989
01:19:58,600 --> 01:20:00,060
- has been delivered.
- Is it over there?

1990
01:20:00,230 --> 01:20:01,330
Over there?

1991
01:20:01,330 --> 01:20:02,530
- Enjoy.
- Thank you for the food.

1992
01:20:02,530 --> 01:20:03,930
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1993
01:20:03,930 --> 01:20:04,930
(Team White returns to their room
after receiving their food.)

1994
01:20:04,930 --> 01:20:06,240
- Enjoy your food.
- Enjoy your food.

1995
01:20:07,600 --> 01:20:10,370
- This is nice.
- The food looks good today.

1996
01:20:10,370 --> 01:20:11,640
- I think our food is here.
- Yes.

1997
01:20:11,710 --> 01:20:12,980
Vector, what are you having?

1998
01:20:13,080 --> 01:20:15,310
- I already ate. Yes.
- Did you?

1999
01:20:16,680 --> 01:20:18,310
By any chance,

2000
01:20:18,620 --> 01:20:20,820
do you know if...

2001
01:20:21,420 --> 01:20:23,020
the pollution level is added
to the resource monitoring?

2002
01:20:23,250 --> 01:20:25,460
Not yet.

2003
01:20:25,460 --> 01:20:27,360
If we can't check, that's not good.

2004
01:20:27,360 --> 01:20:28,390
Exactly.

2005
01:20:29,260 --> 01:20:30,490
Well...

2006
01:20:30,490 --> 01:20:32,730
I'll only tell you.

2007
01:20:33,560 --> 01:20:35,230
There's something called
the pollution credit.

2008
01:20:35,300 --> 01:20:36,400
Pollution?

2009
01:20:36,400 --> 01:20:38,570
We were using the pollution credit
until yesterday.

2010
01:20:38,900 --> 01:20:41,940
Starting today,
we got the pollution-free credit.

2011
01:20:41,940 --> 01:20:44,310
The pollution-free credit
must be more valuable.

2012
01:20:44,310 --> 01:20:45,310
It should be.

2013
01:20:45,310 --> 01:20:47,940
The thing is,
if we use the pollution credit,

2014
01:20:48,010 --> 01:20:50,150
and if it reaches a certain level,

2015
01:20:50,150 --> 01:20:52,020
- everyone's resource...
- Everyone's resource.

2016
01:20:52,020 --> 01:20:53,450
gets deleted.

2017
01:20:54,080 --> 01:20:57,120
If it's developed rapidly,

2018
01:20:57,220 --> 01:20:58,690
it creates air pollution...

2019
01:20:58,690 --> 01:21:00,420
- or environmental pollution.
- Right.

2020
01:21:00,420 --> 01:21:02,730
That'd cut the life in half.

2021
01:21:03,090 --> 01:21:04,990
Right. The life is likely to be affected.

2022
01:21:04,990 --> 01:21:07,560
- Because it's environmental pollution.
- Environmental pollution affects life.

2023
01:21:07,560 --> 01:21:08,930
Then today,

2024
01:21:09,030 --> 01:21:10,870
Team White and Team Red...

2025
01:21:11,970 --> 01:21:13,270
will form an alliance...

2026
01:21:13,670 --> 01:21:17,110
and kill Team Blue.
Get rid of their lives.

2027
01:21:17,270 --> 01:21:19,810
You can survive until tomorrow.

2028
01:21:19,940 --> 01:21:21,310
If there are no variables.

2029
01:21:21,440 --> 01:21:23,380
From what I've seen,

2030
01:21:23,850 --> 01:21:26,280
you shouldn't do anything.

2031
01:21:26,320 --> 01:21:28,050
- Instead of becoming a target?
- Yes.

2032
01:21:28,050 --> 01:21:30,020
Instead of starting a war.

2033
01:21:30,590 --> 01:21:32,360
Actually, if war is declared,

2034
01:21:32,360 --> 01:21:33,460
it's my loss.

2035
01:21:33,960 --> 01:21:35,830
- Because people have to pay diamonds.
- But...

2036
01:21:35,830 --> 01:21:37,290
if Team Blue doesn't sell, it's a war.

2037
01:21:37,290 --> 01:21:38,930
- Right.
- Yes. So...

2038
01:21:39,000 --> 01:21:40,700
- I'll persuade Team Blue...
- Right.

2039
01:21:40,760 --> 01:21:42,300
- If Team Blue doesn't sell...
- They won't be so ruthless.

2040
01:21:42,300 --> 01:21:44,570
- to keep it peaceful.
- Yes.

2041
01:21:44,800 --> 01:21:46,370
- I'll carry this.
- Let's go.

2042
01:21:46,370 --> 01:21:47,740
- See you later.
- Bye.

2043
01:21:48,570 --> 01:21:50,170
I'm still neutral.

2044
01:21:50,270 --> 01:21:53,080
I'll talk to them to maintain peace.

2045
01:21:53,080 --> 01:21:54,880
Is Team Blue skipping lunch?
Why aren't they here?

2046
01:21:54,980 --> 01:21:56,480
I talked to them before.

2047
01:21:56,480 --> 01:21:58,450
They're not interested in food.

2048
01:21:59,220 --> 01:22:01,080
I think they're trying to endure it today.

2049
01:22:01,080 --> 01:22:02,190
That's crazy.

2050
01:22:02,620 --> 01:22:04,220
Team Black...

2051
01:22:04,220 --> 01:22:06,760
He knows everyone's information.

2052
01:22:06,990 --> 01:22:11,160
We need to buy him
to stop him from leaking our information.

2053
01:22:11,160 --> 01:22:12,400
We should be ready...

2054
01:22:12,400 --> 01:22:13,800
to give them one of our lives today.

2055
01:22:13,800 --> 01:22:14,900
For sure.

2056
01:22:14,900 --> 01:22:17,370
If we sell a day's worth,

2057
01:22:17,670 --> 01:22:18,970
- we can sell three lives.
- Yes.

2058
01:22:19,200 --> 01:22:20,840
We can sell 2 and 1.

2059
01:22:20,840 --> 01:22:22,440
By 2 and 1, who are you referring to?

2060
01:22:22,440 --> 01:22:23,670
- Two to Team White,
- Two to Team White,

2061
01:22:23,670 --> 01:22:24,710
- and one to Vector.
- and one to Vector.

2062
01:22:24,710 --> 01:22:26,880
Because we need to win Team Black over.

2063
01:22:27,210 --> 01:22:29,750
Do you want to meet Vector first
to be safe?

2064
01:22:30,210 --> 01:22:32,250
Because that will save us time.

2065
01:22:32,580 --> 01:22:33,680
Right.

2066
01:22:33,680 --> 01:22:34,680
- We can only give him one.
- But...

2067
01:22:34,680 --> 01:22:36,690
we need to think about
what percentage we're going to ask for.

2068
01:22:36,720 --> 01:22:38,220
Twenty percent from a day.

2069
01:22:39,690 --> 01:22:41,460
(Team Blue wants a percentage of
the market sales in return for a life.)

2070
01:22:41,460 --> 01:22:43,160
Even 20 percent is...

2071
01:22:44,090 --> 01:22:46,900
- We're making a concession big time.
- not much for what we're giving.

2072
01:22:47,030 --> 01:22:49,970
Honestly, I think...

2073
01:22:49,970 --> 01:22:52,870
instead of asking a percentage
of the sales,

2074
01:22:52,870 --> 01:22:55,740
we should build a friendship...

2075
01:22:55,740 --> 01:22:57,040
- and receive food.
- We can just...

2076
01:22:57,170 --> 01:22:59,780
Receive food?

2077
01:23:00,210 --> 01:23:02,580
You say this
because you're full right now.

2078
01:23:02,580 --> 01:23:04,080
But when you're hungry...

2079
01:23:04,180 --> 01:23:05,580
and struggling for real...

2080
01:23:05,580 --> 01:23:08,150
I don't mind starving for real.

2081
01:23:08,320 --> 01:23:09,890
Money means more to me.

2082
01:23:09,890 --> 01:23:11,520
- So...
- I prefer money too.

2083
01:23:11,590 --> 01:23:14,790
I have no intention of paying
1,000 dollars for it.

2084
01:23:15,160 --> 01:23:18,490
I actually don't plan to spend it at all.

2085
01:23:18,760 --> 01:23:22,370
Then instead of a percentage,

2086
01:23:22,970 --> 01:23:25,940
we could just demand a set amount.

2087
01:23:26,700 --> 01:23:28,070
Is this lunchtime?

2088
01:23:28,140 --> 01:23:29,440
It's lunchtime right now.

2089
01:23:29,440 --> 01:23:30,840
Do you want to go check it out?

2090
01:23:30,840 --> 01:23:32,440
- Let's go check it out.
- Let's pretend...

2091
01:23:32,440 --> 01:23:34,940
we're checking it out
because we're hungry.

2092
01:23:36,450 --> 01:23:38,310
Is Team Blue not eating?

2093
01:23:40,150 --> 01:23:41,350
Hi.

2094
01:23:41,750 --> 01:23:43,120
- Store owner.
- Vector.

2095
01:23:43,450 --> 01:23:45,290
- Hello.
- How's your business going today?

2096
01:23:45,460 --> 01:23:47,320
- It's going pretty well.
- Good?

2097
01:23:47,990 --> 01:23:49,430
How much are you charging?

2098
01:23:49,430 --> 01:23:51,160
Are you here to shake me down?

2099
01:23:51,190 --> 01:23:52,260
We're here to make an agreement.

2100
01:23:52,260 --> 01:23:54,730
- You are pretty scary.
- No.

2101
01:23:54,730 --> 01:23:56,430
- We...
- You look like thugs.

2102
01:23:56,930 --> 01:23:59,500
You threatened me with my life.

2103
01:23:59,770 --> 01:24:01,470
What did you do for
the productive activities this morning?

2104
01:24:01,640 --> 01:24:04,040
I added items here.

2105
01:24:04,840 --> 01:24:06,540
- Do you have to solve questions?
- So I got Coke Zero.

2106
01:24:07,140 --> 01:24:09,710
- Really?
- I have three packs of pork belly.

2107
01:24:09,710 --> 01:24:11,350
- Coke Zero?
- Coke Zero?

2108
01:24:11,350 --> 01:24:12,420
I see it.

2109
01:24:12,420 --> 01:24:13,920
My goodness.

2110
01:24:13,920 --> 01:24:15,390
- He's clearly smart.
- He's smart.

2111
01:24:15,490 --> 01:24:17,950
How's the price range?

2112
01:24:18,250 --> 01:24:20,990
Each team paid ten.

2113
01:24:21,160 --> 01:24:22,960
- Ten diamonds?
- Yes.

2114
01:24:23,090 --> 01:24:24,960
I was actually thinking...

2115
01:24:24,960 --> 01:24:28,560
about taking half
of your expected sales today.

2116
01:24:28,870 --> 01:24:32,200
If you only got ten from each team,

2117
01:24:32,200 --> 01:24:34,400
we need ten at least.

2118
01:24:34,400 --> 01:24:36,070
That's ridiculous...

2119
01:24:36,070 --> 01:24:39,140
because we got 10 diamonds
for 1 life yesterday from Team White.

2120
01:24:39,140 --> 01:24:40,740
It should be way more expensive.

2121
01:24:40,740 --> 01:24:42,150
- Life's worth more than that now.
- But he hasn't...

2122
01:24:42,150 --> 01:24:44,050
made much yet...

2123
01:24:44,050 --> 01:24:45,180
- But...
- It's too much for him.

2124
01:24:45,180 --> 01:24:48,020
I'll show you how much I've made so far.

2125
01:24:48,550 --> 01:24:50,250
I didn't do anything...

2126
01:24:50,250 --> 01:24:52,360
This is a life.

2127
01:24:52,360 --> 01:24:54,760
We're trading it for a day.

2128
01:24:55,190 --> 01:24:56,730
I'll come clean.

2129
01:24:56,760 --> 01:24:57,760
This is awesome.

2130
01:24:57,760 --> 01:24:59,900
- I didn't see you coming.
- Okay.

2131
01:24:59,930 --> 01:25:01,900
This is all I have. I only have 11.

2132
01:25:03,130 --> 01:25:04,500
This is not easy.

2133
01:25:04,500 --> 01:25:06,100
- I feel...
- Okay.

2134
01:25:06,370 --> 01:25:07,970
At this rate,

2135
01:25:07,970 --> 01:25:09,340
instead of taking them,

2136
01:25:09,340 --> 01:25:10,540
it's better to go with a percentage.

2137
01:25:10,540 --> 01:25:11,910
- For the future.
- But I think...

2138
01:25:11,910 --> 01:25:13,310
food is a good idea too.

2139
01:25:13,310 --> 01:25:15,910
Because the food price will go up.

2140
01:25:16,210 --> 01:25:18,480
- We have to choose one.
- I think the food is only right.

2141
01:25:18,480 --> 01:25:20,250
Keep in mind that we can't take a lot,

2142
01:25:20,250 --> 01:25:22,520
and it could be worth nothing.

2143
01:25:23,150 --> 01:25:25,090
- Those diamonds.
- Right. They might become worthless.

2144
01:25:25,090 --> 01:25:26,460
Right. That's true.

2145
01:25:26,460 --> 01:25:27,660
If...

2146
01:25:28,420 --> 01:25:29,860
you give me a life,

2147
01:25:29,890 --> 01:25:31,060
I'll serve you nicely.

2148
01:25:31,490 --> 01:25:34,500
I think we should trust him on that.

2149
01:25:34,500 --> 01:25:36,370
- Right.
- Let's trust each other.

2150
01:25:36,370 --> 01:25:38,570
- Bring me a life.
- Okay.

2151
01:25:38,570 --> 01:25:40,370
While you're here,

2152
01:25:40,370 --> 01:25:41,800
why don't you take some items?

2153
01:25:42,440 --> 01:25:44,340
- Okay. We...
- What would you like to eat?

2154
01:25:44,440 --> 01:25:46,010
I want to take a lot.

2155
01:25:46,780 --> 01:25:47,810
First, we need soy milk.

2156
01:25:47,810 --> 01:25:48,980
- We need the tofu chips.
- The tofu chips.

2157
01:25:48,980 --> 01:25:50,010
We need the tofu chips.

2158
01:25:50,010 --> 01:25:51,110
This is my favorite.

2159
01:25:51,180 --> 01:25:53,020
Are we having one Coke Zero each?

2160
01:25:53,020 --> 01:25:54,280
Take two eggs?

2161
01:25:54,280 --> 01:25:56,150
- Take two eggs.
- The eggs.

2162
01:25:56,150 --> 01:25:58,290
That's worth 20 diamonds.

2163
01:25:58,390 --> 01:25:59,490
Let's take one more pizza.

2164
01:25:59,490 --> 01:26:00,760
You don't have a microwave.

2165
01:26:00,760 --> 01:26:02,560
Let's save it here then.

2166
01:26:02,560 --> 01:26:04,260
Let's call it a deal.

2167
01:26:04,590 --> 01:26:06,430
We must not get caught.

2168
01:26:09,300 --> 01:26:11,100
No wonder I wanted to wear something big.

2169
01:26:12,340 --> 01:26:13,470
Feel free to take it.

2170
01:26:13,470 --> 01:26:14,640
You'll be fine.

2171
01:26:15,570 --> 01:26:17,310
- Enjoy.
- Thank you.

2172
01:26:17,310 --> 01:26:18,980
- Make sure to give me a life.
- For sure.

2173
01:26:18,980 --> 01:26:20,010
Promise.

2174
01:26:20,210 --> 01:26:23,010
In a way, I tried
some black-market trading.

2175
01:26:23,010 --> 01:26:25,680
My supermarket was written
as Black Market.

2176
01:26:25,680 --> 01:26:27,880
And what is Black Market?
It's for illegal trading.

2177
01:26:28,380 --> 01:26:29,420
So...

2178
01:26:29,420 --> 01:26:30,520
I lived up to my name.

2179
01:26:30,590 --> 01:26:32,120
I don't know how it'll turn out,

2180
01:26:32,120 --> 01:26:35,490
but I tried making a deal outside the law.

2181
01:26:36,290 --> 01:26:37,760
It's worth 1,000 dollars.

2182
01:26:38,160 --> 01:26:40,130
- It looks good.
- Thank you for the food.

2183
01:26:40,130 --> 01:26:41,560
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

2184
01:26:41,560 --> 01:26:42,700
Enjoy.

2185
01:26:46,870 --> 01:26:50,410
Before the price goes up at night,

2186
01:26:50,410 --> 01:26:54,040
should we stock up on the food?

2187
01:26:54,180 --> 01:26:57,410
Actually, I was thinking
it wouldn't be so bad...

2188
01:26:57,510 --> 01:27:00,220
to get a few things for ten diamonds.

2189
01:27:01,280 --> 01:27:03,820
But the currency is way too valuable
right now.

2190
01:27:03,820 --> 01:27:06,560
At this rate, all the diamonds...

2191
01:27:06,860 --> 01:27:08,820
will end up in Team Black's hands.

2192
01:27:08,820 --> 01:27:09,890
That's true.

2193
01:27:10,430 --> 01:27:11,860
So we'll end up issuing...

2194
01:27:11,860 --> 01:27:14,260
more and more...

2195
01:27:14,260 --> 01:27:16,000
to keep the balance.

2196
01:27:16,500 --> 01:27:18,570
That will make the price go up.

2197
01:27:18,900 --> 01:27:21,840
That means more for Team Black.

2198
01:27:21,840 --> 01:27:23,340
Then we'll end up starving.

2199
01:27:23,510 --> 01:27:25,910
I remember, "Increase the money supply..."

2200
01:27:25,910 --> 01:27:28,910
from yesterday. And even today,

2201
01:27:28,910 --> 01:27:31,780
he kept telling us to induce inflation.

2202
01:27:32,250 --> 01:27:34,580
The two things he said keep bothering me.

2203
01:27:34,580 --> 01:27:36,720
- I thought that was strange.
- It was fishy.

2204
01:27:37,050 --> 01:27:38,650
What is Team Black thinking?

2205
01:27:40,190 --> 01:27:42,090
(Dormitory for Team Black)

2206
01:27:43,060 --> 01:27:44,490
I'll go solve it.

2207
01:27:48,500 --> 01:27:51,270
Okay. I got it.

2208
01:27:56,640 --> 01:27:58,980
I'll say that it has nothing to do...

2209
01:27:59,010 --> 01:28:00,580
with the amount of petroleum reserves.

2210
01:28:01,940 --> 01:28:04,750
(No.)

2211
01:28:05,180 --> 01:28:06,350
It's wrong.

2212
01:28:06,420 --> 01:28:08,820
Please pick up a new answer sheet.

2213
01:28:09,020 --> 01:28:10,550
I know it isn't,

2214
01:28:10,550 --> 01:28:11,990
but I'll say it is.

2215
01:28:11,990 --> 01:28:13,790
(Yes.)

2216
01:28:13,790 --> 01:28:15,690
I have to answer it
to turn things in my favor.

2217
01:28:15,690 --> 01:28:16,860
It's wrong.

2218
01:28:16,860 --> 01:28:19,160
(Vector tries to answer
the technique development questions.)

2219
01:28:19,600 --> 01:28:21,500
I'll bring the answers.

2220
01:28:22,230 --> 01:28:23,370
Goodbye.

2221
01:28:29,040 --> 01:28:31,970
The trading for Day Two will begin.

2222
01:28:32,580 --> 01:28:34,880
The residents may ring the bell
in the living room...

2223
01:28:34,910 --> 01:28:39,250
to request another group a meeting.

2224
01:28:39,380 --> 01:28:40,520
Is Team White there?

2225
01:28:40,520 --> 01:28:42,180
- Let's ask for the best.
- Yes.

2226
01:28:42,180 --> 01:28:43,220
Team White?

2227
01:28:44,850 --> 01:28:48,990
I'd like to meet Team White
in the Town Hall.

2228
01:28:50,230 --> 01:28:51,390
Team Blue asked Team White...

2229
01:28:51,530 --> 01:28:52,730
Team Blue asked Team White.

2230
01:28:53,660 --> 01:28:55,130
The request granted.

2231
01:28:55,130 --> 01:28:56,500
Sounds good.

2232
01:28:56,500 --> 01:28:58,070
(The request has been granted.)

2233
01:28:58,400 --> 01:29:00,100
Do we wait in the Town Hall?

2234
01:29:00,100 --> 01:29:01,800
- Do you want to wait there?
- Yes.

2235
01:29:06,340 --> 01:29:08,410
You may declare war...

2236
01:29:08,410 --> 01:29:10,380
during the trading hours starting today.

2237
01:29:10,510 --> 01:29:12,750
Any leaders who want to declare war...

2238
01:29:12,750 --> 01:29:15,720
must pay for the war cost
at the Community Center...

2239
01:29:15,720 --> 01:29:18,090
and declare war.

2240
01:29:19,290 --> 01:29:21,020
The war cost today is...

2241
01:29:21,520 --> 01:29:22,990
How much does it cost?

2242
01:29:22,990 --> 01:29:24,560
- Exactly.
- I'm curious.

2243
01:29:24,560 --> 01:29:26,030
They're going to tell us the war cost.

2244
01:29:30,300 --> 01:29:34,100
The cost of starting a war today
is 15 diamonds.

2245
01:29:34,570 --> 01:29:36,740
- What? That's way too cheap.
- It barely costs anything.

2246
01:29:41,410 --> 01:29:42,710
- That's it?
- That's it?

2247
01:29:45,920 --> 01:29:49,120
Only 15 diamonds to start a war?
That's pretty cheap.

2248
01:29:49,520 --> 01:29:51,590
- It doesn't cost a lot.
- Which means every group can go for it.

2249
01:29:53,290 --> 01:29:56,330
The cost of starting a war
was way too low.

2250
01:29:56,330 --> 01:29:58,790
Think about it.
We were willing to pay eight diamonds...

2251
01:29:58,790 --> 01:30:01,060
just to have dinner.

2252
01:30:01,060 --> 01:30:02,430
But only 15 diamonds?
That's way too cheap.

2253
01:30:02,430 --> 01:30:04,270
If war costs are too low,

2254
01:30:04,270 --> 01:30:05,870
people will declare war recklessly.

2255
01:30:05,870 --> 01:30:07,740
It's probably the cheapest today.
Should we do it today?

2256
01:30:08,540 --> 01:30:10,110
Starting a war is inevitable.

2257
01:30:10,110 --> 01:30:11,510
If it's something we must do
at least once,

2258
01:30:11,510 --> 01:30:13,310
we might as well strike early.

2259
01:30:13,780 --> 01:30:15,510
That's where I stand now.

2260
01:30:16,150 --> 01:30:18,110
We could potentially take 11 lives...

2261
01:30:18,380 --> 01:30:21,080
by only investing 15 diamonds.

2262
01:30:21,880 --> 01:30:22,990
That's pretty good.

2263
01:30:22,990 --> 01:30:23,990
It's an amazing deal.

2264
01:30:24,720 --> 01:30:26,620
It won't be 15 diamonds tomorrow.

2265
01:30:26,620 --> 01:30:27,690
- Probably not.
- Just today.

2266
01:30:27,690 --> 01:30:28,690
- Just today.
- Just today.

2267
01:30:28,690 --> 01:30:30,190
- Just today, right?
- Fifteen diamonds for today.

2268
01:30:30,530 --> 01:30:32,330
So that's 15,000 dollars
out of 200,000 dollars.

2269
01:30:32,330 --> 01:30:35,600
A lot of people commented that
the cost of starting a war was too low.

2270
01:30:35,600 --> 01:30:37,870
But I think it's reasonably priced...

2271
01:30:37,870 --> 01:30:40,400
because wars will keep on happening.

2272
01:30:40,740 --> 01:30:42,470
That's 15,000 dollars.

2273
01:30:42,710 --> 01:30:44,170
That's not a small amount.

2274
01:30:44,310 --> 01:30:45,510
That's enough to buy a car.

2275
01:30:46,210 --> 01:30:49,450
This concludes the announcement
from the Community Center.

2276
01:30:51,080 --> 01:30:53,480
What kind of Community Center is this?

2277
01:30:53,480 --> 01:30:55,080
It's trying to drive a wedge
in the community.

2278
01:30:58,450 --> 01:30:59,620
War? Okay.

2279
01:31:07,060 --> 01:31:08,930
(30 minutes ago)

2280
01:31:09,970 --> 01:31:10,970
Hold on.

2281
01:31:19,240 --> 01:31:20,510
The cost of starting a war...

2282
01:31:23,350 --> 01:31:27,420
(War Cost Determination)

2283
01:31:27,420 --> 01:31:28,550
Fifteen diamonds.

2284
01:31:31,120 --> 01:31:33,520
The cost of war has been set.

2285
01:31:33,520 --> 01:31:35,860
Please determine the cost of the weapon.

2286
01:31:35,860 --> 01:31:40,260
I'll encourage them to start a war.

2287
01:31:40,460 --> 01:31:42,470
They'll pick their weapon...

2288
01:31:42,870 --> 01:31:44,430
after declaring war.

2289
01:31:44,430 --> 01:31:47,300
So weapons should be priced high.

2290
01:31:48,070 --> 01:31:51,510
I'll set 30 diamonds for A,
20 diamonds for B, and 10 diamonds for C.

2291
01:31:52,580 --> 01:31:54,940
The costs of weapons have been set.

2292
01:31:58,310 --> 01:31:59,820
Here's what I'd like to try here.

2293
01:31:59,950 --> 01:32:01,880
In this community,

2294
01:32:01,880 --> 01:32:03,250
rules are set,

2295
01:32:03,250 --> 01:32:05,550
and there's this condition
that we're all playing a game.

2296
01:32:05,550 --> 01:32:06,960
I'd like to betray people...

2297
01:32:06,960 --> 01:32:09,020
and harm others.

2298
01:32:09,020 --> 01:32:11,490
I also want to spread rumors
and throw things into chaos.

2299
01:32:11,490 --> 01:32:13,500
I can try this just for ten days.

2300
01:32:14,100 --> 01:32:15,260
It's going to be so fun.

2301
01:32:16,800 --> 01:32:18,600
(Resident Registration on Day 1)

2302
01:32:19,270 --> 01:32:21,500
Your color is Black.

2303
01:32:21,940 --> 01:32:23,970
There's only one resident in your group.

2304
01:32:23,970 --> 01:32:25,710
By default, you're the leader.

2305
01:32:26,810 --> 01:32:30,780
Team Black will act as a merchant
in the Community Town.

2306
01:32:30,780 --> 01:32:32,280
- A merchant?
- The merchant decides...

2307
01:32:32,280 --> 01:32:35,280
the prices of the items
sold at the supermarket.

2308
01:32:35,780 --> 01:32:39,120
The diamonds acquired through sales
will be the merchant's prize.

2309
01:32:39,460 --> 01:32:40,460
However,

2310
01:32:41,190 --> 01:32:44,960
you have a hidden role, Vector.

2311
01:32:45,130 --> 01:32:46,130
What is it?

2312
01:32:47,660 --> 01:32:50,300
Please read the following command,

2313
01:32:50,300 --> 01:32:53,340
and you'll find out your real role.

2314
01:32:53,340 --> 01:32:55,000
What is it? Say what?

2315
01:32:55,200 --> 01:32:57,540
(Command)

2316
01:32:57,740 --> 01:32:59,540
"The truth of the weapon dealer..."

2317
01:32:59,880 --> 01:33:01,980
"placed within secret room of center."

2318
01:33:10,120 --> 01:33:12,220
This is it, right? Gosh, no way.

2319
01:33:12,490 --> 01:33:13,490
My gosh.

2320
01:33:14,160 --> 01:33:15,660
Goodness, this is crazy.

2321
01:33:15,660 --> 01:33:17,130
"A weapon dealer?"

2322
01:33:18,030 --> 01:33:20,060
(The Rules for the Weapon Dealer)

2323
01:33:21,000 --> 01:33:22,160
Oh, my.

2324
01:33:24,230 --> 01:33:27,500
You're a weapon dealer
of the Community House.

2325
01:33:28,400 --> 01:33:31,340
The residents believe that
your prize money will come...

2326
01:33:31,340 --> 01:33:33,710
from the sales at the supermarket.

2327
01:33:34,340 --> 01:33:38,550
The weapon dealer's prize money
will solely come...

2328
01:33:38,550 --> 01:33:40,520
from the war costs and weapon sales.

2329
01:33:40,520 --> 01:33:43,490
"More wars yield bigger prize money."

2330
01:33:43,790 --> 01:33:45,120
I have to turn them against each other.

2331
01:33:45,120 --> 01:33:47,390
It's on the house. Help yourselves.

2332
01:33:47,720 --> 01:33:50,160
Tell me which one you want.
You can choose from this selection.

2333
01:33:50,160 --> 01:33:52,730
(He provided the food for free
from the first day.)

2334
01:33:53,630 --> 01:33:57,570
(The weapon dealer can't take the sales
from the supermarket.)

2335
01:33:57,830 --> 01:34:00,070
On the surface,

2336
01:34:00,070 --> 01:34:03,370
I want to keep playing
the generous supermarket owner.

2337
01:34:03,570 --> 01:34:08,340
But there may come a moment
where things change rather drastically.

2338
01:34:08,340 --> 01:34:10,310
It will be when wars keep happening...

2339
01:34:10,310 --> 01:34:12,150
and the diamonds become more valuable.

2340
01:34:12,150 --> 01:34:15,780
The weapon dealer can check
each group's total resources.

2341
01:34:15,780 --> 01:34:16,990
They got two more.

2342
01:34:18,850 --> 01:34:20,760
The weapon dealer can monitor...

2343
01:34:20,760 --> 01:34:22,790
and wiretap each group's living room.

2344
01:34:24,830 --> 01:34:27,960
No one built up a good rapport
better than Vector yesterday.

2345
01:34:27,960 --> 01:34:30,000
- He did a great job with that.
- Yes.

2346
01:34:30,000 --> 01:34:32,530
He went around
and talked to every single group.

2347
01:34:33,340 --> 01:34:35,700
(A wiretapping device is hidden
in the living room.)

2348
01:34:36,510 --> 01:34:38,470
Acting in good faith is very important.

2349
01:34:38,470 --> 01:34:40,910
The longer this goes on,
having a good rapport...

2350
01:34:40,910 --> 01:34:44,650
I acquired several important clues.

2351
01:34:44,650 --> 01:34:47,580
For instance, I got to hear
their honest thoughts.

2352
01:34:47,580 --> 01:34:49,590
If a war breaks out,
so many people will get eliminated.

2353
01:34:49,590 --> 01:34:50,850
- Right.
- Yes.

2354
01:34:50,850 --> 01:34:52,490
Is it a good idea to start a war...

2355
01:34:52,490 --> 01:34:53,890
until that happens?

2356
01:34:53,890 --> 01:34:56,160
Every team is suspicious of me.

2357
01:34:56,160 --> 01:34:58,760
I don't think Vector will have to use...

2358
01:34:58,760 --> 01:35:01,530
- the diamonds to get the supplies.
- Right.

2359
01:35:01,530 --> 01:35:04,870
Collecting as many diamonds as possible...

2360
01:35:04,870 --> 01:35:06,000
That sounds one-dimensional.

2361
01:35:06,000 --> 01:35:08,140
I'm sure there's something else
underneath that.

2362
01:35:09,270 --> 01:35:12,740
Team Red is suspecting me the most.

2363
01:35:12,740 --> 01:35:14,210
That was so nerve-racking.

2364
01:35:14,210 --> 01:35:15,780
Once they open the door and walk in,

2365
01:35:15,780 --> 01:35:17,810
they can see that
I'm listening to their conversations.

2366
01:35:17,810 --> 01:35:19,980
And there was a card
for the weapon dealer.

2367
01:35:19,980 --> 01:35:21,720
So I took it off.

2368
01:35:21,720 --> 01:35:23,350
Either way, I have to use the room...

2369
01:35:23,350 --> 01:35:24,950
during the break
or while the snack bar is open.

2370
01:35:24,950 --> 01:35:27,620
When I'm wearing the headset,
I might suddenly hear a voice.

2371
01:35:27,620 --> 01:35:29,260
Then I need to listen to that.
So I take it off for a bit.

2372
01:35:29,260 --> 01:35:30,560
The Town Hall is open.

2373
01:35:30,560 --> 01:35:32,360
So anyone can walk in at any time.

2374
01:35:33,030 --> 01:35:34,900
I need to turn off the TV.

2375
01:35:36,670 --> 01:35:38,730
My position isn't all exciting,

2376
01:35:39,170 --> 01:35:40,840
which I thought it would be at first.

2377
01:35:40,970 --> 01:35:42,200
Were you productive?

2378
01:35:42,200 --> 01:35:43,270
Yes, I was.

2379
01:35:43,970 --> 01:35:46,540
What were you able to produce?

2380
01:35:46,540 --> 01:35:48,140
I had to produce these supplies.

2381
01:35:48,140 --> 01:35:50,650
- So you get actual goods in return?
- That's right.

2382
01:35:50,650 --> 01:35:53,380
I got pork belly and Coke Zero.

2383
01:35:54,350 --> 01:35:55,920
I made up a bunch of lies.

2384
01:35:55,920 --> 01:35:57,920
"I got these supplies
through my productive activity."

2385
01:35:57,920 --> 01:36:00,120
"I'm working hard for our community."

2386
01:36:00,120 --> 01:36:03,390
I wanted to emphasize that,
so I made up a productive activity...

2387
01:36:03,390 --> 01:36:05,060
I didn't even do and shared it.

2388
01:36:05,960 --> 01:36:08,030
Moreover, there are puzzles...

2389
01:36:08,030 --> 01:36:11,500
in the residents' dormitories that
reveal the identity of the weapon dealer.

2390
01:36:12,500 --> 01:36:14,070
- What are those numbers for?
- If all the residents...

2391
01:36:14,070 --> 01:36:15,640
- put together their information...
- Three, five, one...

2392
01:36:15,640 --> 01:36:17,140
- and solve all the puzzles...
- Two, four,

2393
01:36:17,140 --> 01:36:19,370
one, four.
Add three to the sixth power to that.

2394
01:36:19,710 --> 01:36:21,310
Two hundred and five. Who's good at math?

2395
01:36:21,310 --> 01:36:22,380
- Are you good at math?
- No.

2396
01:36:22,850 --> 01:36:25,650
Then the weapon dealer's secret safe
will be exposed.

2397
01:36:26,550 --> 01:36:30,390
The military funds collected
up to that point will be wiped out.

2398
01:36:34,420 --> 01:36:38,460
"The answer to the puzzle is the command
you speak to enter the room."

2399
01:36:38,990 --> 01:36:40,460
I'm glad I wrote that down.

2400
01:36:41,060 --> 01:36:44,430
"The truth of the weapon dealer
placed within secret room..."

2401
01:36:45,330 --> 01:36:48,040
"Secret room of center." That's here.

2402
01:36:49,270 --> 01:36:53,440
The weapon dealer has an ally
who has disguised...

2403
01:36:53,440 --> 01:36:55,580
as a resident.

2404
01:36:56,980 --> 01:36:58,550
Hold on.

2405
01:36:58,980 --> 01:37:03,050
The ally can only receive
half of the weapon dealer's prize money.

2406
01:37:03,050 --> 01:37:05,150
When the ally gets eliminated,

2407
01:37:05,150 --> 01:37:08,690
the weapon dealer's final prize money
will be halved.

2408
01:37:10,890 --> 01:37:12,330
I have to protect the ally,
no matter what.

2409
01:37:13,060 --> 01:37:15,360
"In war, what is sacrificed first?"

2410
01:37:15,360 --> 01:37:17,830
The one who asks you this question...

2411
01:37:17,830 --> 01:37:20,340
is your ally.

2412
01:37:20,840 --> 01:37:22,840
Your answer to the question is "Truth."

2413
01:37:22,840 --> 01:37:25,010
That's your secret contact code.

2414
01:37:25,070 --> 01:37:28,680
Use your ally to cause conflicts
in the groups.

2415
01:37:28,680 --> 01:37:31,810
(Use your ally to cause conflicts
in the groups.)

2416
01:37:33,620 --> 01:37:37,450
"Placed within secret room of center."

2417
01:37:37,750 --> 01:37:39,190
"Secret room of center."

2418
01:37:39,690 --> 01:37:42,260
"Placed within secret room of center."

2419
01:37:43,930 --> 01:37:45,630
I need to stop them
from solving the puzzles.

2420
01:37:45,630 --> 01:37:47,030
I wonder if I can pull this off.

2421
01:37:50,500 --> 01:37:53,040
- Wait. Is it "secret room of center?"
- Three.

2422
01:37:53,170 --> 01:37:54,700
Is there a secret room in the Center?

2423
01:37:54,700 --> 01:37:55,840
In the Community Center?

2424
01:37:57,110 --> 01:37:58,110
Can't we go to the Center now?

2425
01:37:58,110 --> 01:37:59,110
Now?

2426
01:38:01,040 --> 01:38:03,210
Is it "secret room of center?"

2427
01:38:03,210 --> 01:38:06,110
I noticed a code in the dormitory.

2428
01:38:07,680 --> 01:38:09,790
Anyone would've found that suspicious.

2429
01:38:10,590 --> 01:38:11,720
I wanted to solve it fast.

2430
01:38:12,590 --> 01:38:13,720
There were six numbers.

2431
01:38:15,060 --> 01:38:16,630
I can group them by three.

2432
01:38:16,630 --> 01:38:17,960
And there are 18 of them.

2433
01:38:19,060 --> 01:38:21,360
I followed this order. Then I got...

2434
01:38:22,200 --> 01:38:24,500
I had 6 fragments of 3 letters.

2435
01:38:25,800 --> 01:38:28,940
I thought following the order
would give me a sentence.

2436
01:38:29,710 --> 01:38:33,240
So the phrase we got was
"secret room of center."

2437
01:38:34,640 --> 01:38:36,310
We need to find it fast.

2438
01:38:36,910 --> 01:38:38,810
We need to find it really fast.

2439
01:38:39,480 --> 01:38:41,420
There's something we have to take care of.

2440
01:38:42,780 --> 01:38:45,420
I'm so curious.
The curiosity is killing me.

2441
01:38:46,360 --> 01:38:48,820
What's that thing on the right?

2442
01:38:49,190 --> 01:38:50,360
It looks suspicious, right?

2443
01:38:50,830 --> 01:38:52,060
(Team Red searched through the Center
from Day One.)

2444
01:38:52,060 --> 01:38:53,060
Is that the place?

2445
01:38:54,000 --> 01:38:55,000
We must hurry.

2446
01:38:55,000 --> 01:38:56,230
(Day 1, evening)

2447
01:38:57,000 --> 01:38:59,470
Clearly, this looks very suspicious.

2448
01:38:59,470 --> 01:39:01,840
It won't rotate, right?

2449
01:39:01,840 --> 01:39:03,040
(Day 1, dawn)

2450
01:39:03,870 --> 01:39:05,070
It's closed.

2451
01:39:05,070 --> 01:39:06,880
- It's over for the day.
- It's closed.

2452
01:39:07,340 --> 01:39:09,880
It made me wonder
if the code was in other rooms too.

2453
01:39:09,880 --> 01:39:11,380
So I asked around.

2454
01:39:11,380 --> 01:39:14,350
Did you guys solve the code on the wall?

2455
01:39:14,750 --> 01:39:15,820
We didn't get to that yet.

2456
01:39:15,820 --> 01:39:17,020
- You didn't?
- No.

2457
01:39:17,190 --> 01:39:18,550
- Wasn't there...
- Yes?

2458
01:39:18,550 --> 01:39:20,720
extra information on the wall?

2459
01:39:22,260 --> 01:39:25,090
Extra information?
I didn't get a chance to look around.

2460
01:39:28,530 --> 01:39:30,000
I should hurry. I'm going to solve it.

2461
01:39:31,100 --> 01:39:32,100
My honey jar.

2462
01:39:33,800 --> 01:39:34,900
One, two, three.

2463
01:39:35,470 --> 01:39:36,610
How do I open this?

2464
01:39:38,210 --> 01:39:40,740
The only center in our town...

2465
01:39:40,740 --> 01:39:42,510
is the Community Center.

2466
01:39:42,710 --> 01:39:44,110
I kept looking.

2467
01:39:44,110 --> 01:39:45,580
But there was no secret room.

2468
01:39:45,580 --> 01:39:47,020
I didn't see anything
resembling a secret room.

2469
01:39:47,480 --> 01:39:49,150
I need to stop them
from solving the puzzles.

2470
01:39:49,690 --> 01:39:50,990
I wanted to solve it fast.

2471
01:39:50,990 --> 01:39:54,220
(The one trying to keep it hidden,
the one trying to find it)

2472
01:39:54,220 --> 01:39:57,660
(The Community 2: Invisible Hand)

2473
01:40:32,730 --> 01:40:34,330
(The Community 2: Invisible Hand)
